1
00:02:26,446 --> 00:02:32,805
I said even the eagle in
the sky cannot sense me.

2
00:02:33,046 --> 00:02:37,405
You didn't find us, I turned
your best one to a bait.

3
00:02:37,646 --> 00:02:40,725
I lured the wolf into the trap.

4
00:02:53,406 --> 00:02:57,285
We have not lost our minds to hold...

5
00:02:57,286 --> 00:03:00,485
...the hand of friendship you extended...

6
00:03:00,926 --> 00:03:03,685
What kind of dog are you that...

7
00:03:03,686 --> 00:03:06,365
..you attack my castles..

8
00:03:07,166 --> 00:03:11,005
...where you came as a guest? You came and...

9
00:03:11,006 --> 00:03:15,005
...abducted my Shahzade and my Bey.

10
00:03:15,006 --> 00:03:18,365
What kind of dog are you?

11
00:03:18,366 --> 00:03:22,045
While sharing my meal...

12
00:03:22,886 --> 00:03:26,845
...you tried to poison the people.

13
00:03:27,126 --> 00:03:32,925
Traitor, treacherous, jackal,
you call these names to us.

14
00:03:32,926 --> 00:03:35,565
But you call yourselves glorious, brave and...

15
00:03:35,566 --> 00:03:37,845
..powerful.

16
00:03:37,846 --> 00:03:41,245
Is that so, Osman? -Right...

17
00:03:41,246 --> 00:03:43,245
Of course.

18
00:03:43,246 --> 00:03:47,885
The reputation and honor of a valiant...

19
00:03:47,886 --> 00:03:49,885
...come from the path they walk.

20
00:03:49,886 --> 00:03:51,805
But for people like you..

21
00:03:51,806 --> 00:03:57,685
...your path is only arrogance and heedlessness.

22
00:03:57,686 --> 00:04:01,085
Ah, your arrogance...

23
00:04:01,126 --> 00:04:04,325
It's this arrogance that
has brought you to this state.

24
00:04:04,366 --> 00:04:06,805
Faithless dog.

25
00:04:07,646 --> 00:04:10,845
Faithless dog.

26
00:04:11,206 --> 00:04:13,645
You will get even more pale.

27
00:04:14,126 --> 00:04:16,605
The poison running in your blood...

28
00:04:16,606 --> 00:04:18,485
...will break your legs.

29
00:04:18,486 --> 00:04:21,084
You will kneel before me, Osman.

30
00:04:23,366 --> 00:04:25,365
You will kneel.

31
00:04:32,206 --> 00:04:33,925
My Fatma..

32
00:04:33,926 --> 00:04:36,085
My beautiful daughter.

33
00:04:44,766 --> 00:04:46,165
Mother..

34
00:04:46,366 --> 00:04:48,125
Did my brother..

35
00:04:48,126 --> 00:04:51,885
...come?
He will come, my daughter.

36
00:04:51,886 --> 00:04:55,245
He will come, don't worry.

37
00:04:57,046 --> 00:05:02,205
Cover yourself. Come on.
-Mother...

38
00:05:03,206 --> 00:05:05,085
Mother don't leave...

39
00:05:14,846 --> 00:05:15,885
Meryem...

40
00:05:27,246 --> 00:05:30,085
You say "mother" in such a way that Meryem...

41
00:05:30,086 --> 00:05:35,445
...your voice puts out the old fire in me.

42
00:05:38,206 --> 00:05:42,125
Your face, your eyes...

43
00:05:43,686 --> 00:05:45,565
It's like a dream.

44
00:05:49,206 --> 00:05:54,005
I feel like my daughter who will
never grow up is right next to me.

45
00:05:57,406 --> 00:06:01,325
You have a fever.
You have a fever.

46
00:06:24,246 --> 00:06:28,845
Mine was just a dream..

47
00:06:31,806 --> 00:06:34,645
You are someone else's wounded bird.

48
00:07:10,766 --> 00:07:14,045
I am here to protect you...

49
00:07:14,046 --> 00:07:16,765
...but I cannot do anything.

50
00:07:20,246 --> 00:07:22,885
My Allah, give us power..

51
00:07:23,126 --> 00:07:26,085
Give us power...

52
00:07:26,086 --> 00:07:31,645
Give us power to resist.

53
00:07:31,646 --> 00:07:33,765
Give us power..

54
00:07:33,766 --> 00:07:35,565
Nokers(Mongolian Soldiers)!

55
00:07:35,606 --> 00:07:37,405
My Bey!

56
00:07:37,846 --> 00:07:39,645
My Bey!

57
00:07:55,646 --> 00:07:58,805
I will never fall! Never!

58
00:07:59,166 --> 00:08:04,045
-I will never kneel before the infidel.
-You will!

59
00:08:04,046 --> 00:08:06,285
I said you will!

60
00:08:06,286 --> 00:08:09,405
You will do as I say, or..

61
00:08:09,406 --> 00:08:14,433
...your son Orhan and the
other dog will beg me to kill them.

62
00:08:14,445 --> 00:08:16,125
Never!

63
00:08:16,406 --> 00:08:19,005
I will never kneel!

64
00:08:22,086 --> 00:08:25,805
No one can make me kneel!

65
00:08:26,326 --> 00:08:27,845
Faithless dog!

66
00:08:31,046 --> 00:08:33,485
Look at me!

67
00:08:33,566 --> 00:08:40,125
We did not beg to live, nor did we beg to die.

68
00:08:42,446 --> 00:08:51,365
If we are going to die by the sword
of the infidel, sure we will, but...

69
00:08:51,526 --> 00:08:55,485
Death does not disgrace us.

70
00:08:55,486 --> 00:08:56,565
Never!

71
00:08:56,846 --> 00:09:01,085
But our lands will never face defeat.

72
00:09:04,526 --> 00:09:05,885
They will, Osman

73
00:09:07,926 --> 00:09:09,485
They will.

74
00:09:09,846 --> 00:09:13,485
If you are not going to give up your state

75
00:09:14,246 --> 00:09:19,645
for your own life or for your children,
you will do so for the lives of your people

76
00:09:22,006 --> 00:09:27,925
The poison in your veins is
not only in the wells of your tribe,

77
00:09:27,926 --> 00:09:35,965
but also in Sogut, Mekece,
Akhisar, all your lands.

78
00:09:37,926 --> 00:09:46,565
Only a treacherous being who does not trust
his own strength like you would do this!

79
00:09:46,566 --> 00:09:51,085
As long as your stubbornness
and impertinence continue,

80
00:09:51,086 --> 00:09:56,165
you will not get this antidote
from me and your Hatun

81
00:09:56,246 --> 00:10:03,285
your children, your army, your people

82
00:10:04,486 --> 00:10:07,205
They will die one by one.

83
00:10:09,046 --> 00:10:11,325
What do you want from me?

84
00:10:23,086 --> 00:10:27,565
You will visit everywhere in
your tribe and land with me.

85
00:10:27,566 --> 00:10:29,805
You will bow down to Mongols.

86
00:10:29,806 --> 00:10:32,605
You will surrender, willingly.

87
00:10:33,446 --> 00:10:38,125
And you will let your people
hear that you surrendered.

88
00:10:44,806 --> 00:10:47,165
Mother...

89
00:10:47,166 --> 00:10:50,605
Mother...
-I am alright. I am alright.

90
00:10:51,046 --> 00:10:53,165
I am alright. I am...

91
00:10:54,126 --> 00:10:55,325
I am alright.

92
00:10:55,326 --> 00:10:58,685
Mother, you are ill. You need to take a rest.

93
00:10:58,686 --> 00:11:02,045
You are getting weaker.
-I am alright.

94
00:11:02,046 --> 00:11:05,125
How is the situation, my son?
Couldn't you find the antidote?

95
00:11:05,126 --> 00:11:07,605
They are all in a fever.

96
00:11:10,926 --> 00:11:13,245
The news is not good, mother.

97
00:11:13,606 --> 00:11:16,205
Not just the tribe...

98
00:11:16,206 --> 00:11:19,120
People started to
show the effects of the

99
00:11:19,132 --> 00:11:22,685
poisoning in Sogut,
Yenisehir and in all our lands.

100
00:11:23,046 --> 00:11:25,085
They poisoned them as well.

101
00:11:25,086 --> 00:11:27,605
What are you saying, Alaeddin?

102
00:11:28,126 --> 00:11:31,085
We need a solution, Alaeddin.

103
00:11:31,086 --> 00:11:32,965
What about Osman?

104
00:11:34,006 --> 00:11:37,205
The enemies have the antidote.

105
00:11:41,126 --> 00:11:45,525
The elderly and children are the most affected.

106
00:11:45,526 --> 00:11:47,325
But...

107
00:11:50,886 --> 00:11:53,885
...Alps are also losing their power, mother.

108
00:11:54,726 --> 00:11:57,045
We are losing our strength.

109
00:11:57,046 --> 00:11:59,365
It's such a poison that...

110
00:11:59,566 --> 00:12:02,965
...it kills people from the inside slowly.

111
00:12:03,446 --> 00:12:06,165
I can slow its effect.

112
00:12:06,646 --> 00:12:08,685
But I cannot cure it, mother.

113
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:10,645
We will not give up, my son.

114
00:12:10,646 --> 00:12:14,165
I will stand tall until you find the antidote.

115
00:12:14,166 --> 00:12:15,765
We will find it.

116
00:12:15,766 --> 00:12:19,525
-We will find it, my son.
-God willing, mother.

117
00:12:22,206 --> 00:12:26,565
Mother... Mother, don't leave.

118
00:12:35,206 --> 00:12:36,845
If she were alive

119
00:12:38,526 --> 00:12:41,125
...Halime would be at this age now.

120
00:12:42,966 --> 00:12:47,885
Let me see your face once, mother.

121
00:12:51,926 --> 00:12:54,125
It's all dark, mother.

122
00:12:55,286 --> 00:12:57,925
It's all dark.

123
00:13:12,686 --> 00:13:14,725
Bala Hatun.

124
00:13:16,966 --> 00:13:18,925
You don't look well.

125
00:13:19,806 --> 00:13:22,805
I got some healing herbs boiled. Drink.

126
00:13:23,846 --> 00:13:25,245
No!

127
00:13:30,566 --> 00:13:32,565
Don't drink anything she gives, mother.

128
00:13:33,166 --> 00:13:35,485
She may harm you.

129
00:13:39,326 --> 00:13:43,085
-We can't trust Begum Hatun.
-What are you talking about, Gonca?

130
00:13:55,126 --> 00:13:57,405
You know me well.

131
00:13:57,886 --> 00:14:00,285
And those who know me know this.

132
00:14:01,006 --> 00:14:07,285
As long as I keep breathing,

133
00:14:08,926 --> 00:14:13,205
I and the men following me will never stop...

134
00:14:13,806 --> 00:14:17,365
...before we take revenge
from you and people like you.

135
00:14:21,646 --> 00:14:23,405
Even in this situation

136
00:14:23,606 --> 00:14:26,605
...you still keep being arrogant.

137
00:14:26,966 --> 00:14:32,165
What you call arrogance is my honor and glory.

138
00:14:32,446 --> 00:14:34,725
It's what you lack.

139
00:14:35,046 --> 00:14:40,805
You have only arrogance and failure.

140
00:14:47,966 --> 00:14:52,125
-It's easy to kill you.
Stay away from my Bey, you dog

141
00:14:55,166 --> 00:14:58,885
You made up a cause and spread it in the hearts.

142
00:14:59,086 --> 00:15:01,845
Yet I will take it off from the hearts.

143
00:15:04,806 --> 00:15:06,765
It's easy to die.

144
00:15:07,326 --> 00:15:12,125
But I will make you and your
nation slaves of Mongolians.

145
00:15:12,526 --> 00:15:14,125
Turks...

146
00:15:15,446 --> 00:15:17,165
...neither kneel..

147
00:15:17,446 --> 00:15:20,765
...nor serve the servants!

148
00:15:22,526 --> 00:15:24,485
You and your nation...

149
00:15:25,126 --> 00:15:28,925
...will be whatever I desire.

150
00:15:29,246 --> 00:15:31,845
Nokers (Mongolian Soldier), take the cage.

151
00:16:15,126 --> 00:16:16,325
Stop!

152
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:23,285
Go to your tribe and see!

153
00:16:23,646 --> 00:16:27,525
See and kneel before me..

154
00:16:27,766 --> 00:16:29,685
...to save your people

155
00:16:29,766 --> 00:16:33,005
I will be your death.

156
00:16:33,286 --> 00:16:36,085
I will be your butcher.

157
00:16:39,686 --> 00:16:41,645
You can't run off, Osman.

158
00:16:43,006 --> 00:16:44,645
You can't run off.

159
00:16:45,526 --> 00:16:50,605
Even if you run away from
this, you can't escape your fate.

160
00:16:53,766 --> 00:16:55,765
Tell me what's going on.

161
00:16:58,566 --> 00:17:01,305
Gonca is angry with me. She
doesn't know what she says..

162
00:17:01,305 --> 00:17:02,565
Shut up, Begum!

163
00:17:03,006 --> 00:17:04,565
You can't deceive me.

164
00:17:04,846 --> 00:17:08,125
Your aide Guldane confessed
everything before she died.

165
00:17:08,526 --> 00:17:10,685
She confessed what, Gonca?

166
00:17:11,006 --> 00:17:14,365
All the evil actions in the tribe
were performed by Begum.

167
00:17:15,204 --> 00:17:19,925
It was her who turned us against
each other and made evil plans.

168
00:17:23,646 --> 00:17:27,005
We protected you.

169
00:17:27,406 --> 00:17:29,885
We looked after you and gave you duties.

170
00:17:30,326 --> 00:17:33,165
Why did you do that, Begum?

171
00:17:33,286 --> 00:17:37,165
-It's a slander.
-I'm not done yet, Begum.

172
00:17:40,646 --> 00:17:44,325
Because she wants to put you in trouble, mother.

173
00:17:46,006 --> 00:17:49,125
Because Begum Hatun...

174
00:17:52,446 --> 00:17:55,325
...loves Osman Bey.

175
00:18:08,606 --> 00:18:12,965
Is this how you return my favors, Gonca?

176
00:18:13,086 --> 00:18:14,205
Favors?

177
00:18:15,566 --> 00:18:17,685
You didn't do me favors, Begum.

178
00:18:18,246 --> 00:18:19,965
You just cared about yourself.

179
00:18:21,286 --> 00:18:23,925
You wanted to make me turn against my family.

180
00:18:24,566 --> 00:18:30,725
In fact, your biggest purpose
was to hurt my mother, right?

181
00:18:31,926 --> 00:18:36,045
You were going to hit me
through my children, huh?

182
00:18:36,566 --> 00:18:38,045
I told you before.

183
00:18:38,166 --> 00:18:42,285
I told you that your undue
bravery would cost your life.

184
00:18:43,046 --> 00:18:44,885
I didn't make a mistake.

185
00:18:49,326 --> 00:18:54,165
I fell in love with Osman Bey long before you.

186
00:18:58,166 --> 00:18:59,925
Love?

187
00:19:00,846 --> 00:19:02,325
Love, huh?

188
00:19:03,286 --> 00:19:06,205
What do you know about love?

189
00:19:08,606 --> 00:19:11,045
Osman Bey is my love.

190
00:19:11,886 --> 00:19:14,685
Yours is just a dark stain.

191
00:19:15,526 --> 00:19:17,885
There is no place for that stain, Begum.

192
00:19:18,366 --> 00:19:22,045
You can't dishonor love
with your poisonous tongue.

193
00:19:23,606 --> 00:19:25,525
You're confused...

194
00:19:27,126 --> 00:19:28,565
..about love.

195
00:19:29,606 --> 00:19:32,565
You thought it was
ambition... Such an ambition...

196
00:19:33,046 --> 00:19:35,325
...that the fire burned the whole tribe.

197
00:19:35,486 --> 00:19:39,165
What do you mean?

198
00:19:40,926 --> 00:19:42,685
Everyone is poisoned, Begum.

199
00:19:43,046 --> 00:19:45,205
And why are you not?

200
00:19:45,286 --> 00:19:47,005
You blame me for this too?

201
00:19:47,206 --> 00:19:49,845
You're looking for one to execute.

202
00:19:50,086 --> 00:19:52,965
My only mistake was falling in love.
-Enough!

203
00:19:53,726 --> 00:19:56,805
Pack up your things and leave this tribe.

204
00:19:56,886 --> 00:19:59,405
I don't want you here. You have to leave.

205
00:20:01,286 --> 00:20:03,885
You can't kick me out.

206
00:20:05,766 --> 00:20:09,285
As long as Osman Bey doesn't kick me out,
I am not going anywhere!

207
00:20:16,646 --> 00:20:18,085
What, Bala?

208
00:20:18,566 --> 00:20:20,445
Are you not confident?

209
00:20:22,406 --> 00:20:24,005
Are you afraid of me?

210
00:20:26,326 --> 00:20:28,085
Afraid, huh?

211
00:20:29,166 --> 00:20:31,085
You can't scare me, Begum.

212
00:20:32,046 --> 00:20:34,285
Either you will go yourself...

213
00:20:34,646 --> 00:20:36,725
...or I know how to kick you out.

214
00:20:37,046 --> 00:20:41,925
Even if everybody obeys
you in this tribe, I won't.

215
00:20:43,006 --> 00:20:46,805
And I'm not going anywhere just
because you're telling me to leave.

216
00:20:46,846 --> 00:20:49,445
Osman Bey invited me to this tribe.

217
00:21:00,166 --> 00:21:02,245
I won't go anywhere without his order.

218
00:21:02,366 --> 00:21:06,045
Don't you mention my
husband's name again, hatun.

219
00:21:07,166 --> 00:21:10,165
I said what I said.

220
00:21:10,566 --> 00:21:12,645
Next time, my sword will speak.

221
00:21:13,166 --> 00:21:14,965
Get out of my sight!

222
00:21:17,366 --> 00:21:18,245
Mother.

223
00:21:21,445 --> 00:21:22,445
You're good.

224
00:21:23,126 --> 00:21:24,805
You're good.

225
00:21:51,766 --> 00:21:53,605
-My Bey.
-My Bey.

226
00:21:54,246 --> 00:21:57,005
-Warriors.
-Thanks to Allah.

227
00:21:57,926 --> 00:21:59,725
We were looking for you, my Bey.

228
00:22:01,206 --> 00:22:02,965
Orhan Bey and Boran Bey.

229
00:22:03,326 --> 00:22:09,045
-Any news?
-We looked everywhere and followed every trail.

230
00:22:09,806 --> 00:22:11,485
But we couldn't find.

231
00:22:14,086 --> 00:22:18,045
We left the alps who were in bad
condition in a tribe nearby, my Bey.

232
00:22:18,446 --> 00:22:21,845
But all the tribes have the same problem.

233
00:22:23,406 --> 00:22:25,365
They poisoned all the water.

234
00:22:25,446 --> 00:22:26,845
People are sick.

235
00:22:27,086 --> 00:22:28,525
They're dying, my Bey.

236
00:22:30,686 --> 00:22:35,245
Inform all the healers
in all of our lands, Aykurt.

237
00:22:35,566 --> 00:22:38,205
-As you order, my Bey.
-Here we go.

238
00:22:38,366 --> 00:22:40,925
People shouldn't fall weaker.

239
00:22:41,526 --> 00:22:43,405
-We're going to our tribe.
-My Bey.

240
00:22:43,886 --> 00:22:47,365
Will we stop looking for
Shahzade Orhan and Boran Bey?

241
00:22:47,686 --> 00:22:49,565
The owl called Ulugan...

242
00:22:50,246 --> 00:22:55,885
...can't harm my son or
Boran without my knowledge.

243
00:22:56,126 --> 00:22:57,525
Don't worry.

244
00:22:57,806 --> 00:23:02,085
Don't worry.
We're going to our tribe.

245
00:23:02,166 --> 00:23:04,085
Come on!

246
00:23:15,486 --> 00:23:16,885
Orhan.

247
00:23:24,486 --> 00:23:26,925
I was just with your father.

248
00:23:27,846 --> 00:23:31,605
You should know your life
doesn't matter at all to him.

249
00:23:31,966 --> 00:23:34,165
What are you talking about, dog?

250
00:23:34,846 --> 00:23:36,925
Kill me if you desire.

251
00:23:37,686 --> 00:23:40,245
Stop playing game like kids!

252
00:23:46,566 --> 00:23:49,285
Your father spoke the same.

253
00:23:49,686 --> 00:23:52,765
All his people are about to die of poison.

254
00:23:53,886 --> 00:23:56,645
But he still keeps his tail upright.

255
00:23:58,726 --> 00:24:03,565
This arrogance of yours will destroy you.

256
00:24:04,046 --> 00:24:07,765
You're going to die because of your father.

257
00:24:08,166 --> 00:24:10,045
Whatever my father does

258
00:24:10,486 --> 00:24:12,445
...he does the best.

259
00:24:12,846 --> 00:24:17,685
I'd sacrifice myself even
if I had a thousand lives!

260
00:24:19,446 --> 00:24:21,525
But you should know this, dog.

261
00:24:21,886 --> 00:24:24,445
We weren't born to be captives.

262
00:24:24,686 --> 00:24:30,125
Neither my father nor I will ever...

263
00:24:30,886 --> 00:24:33,045
...kneel before a dog like you.

264
00:24:38,726 --> 00:24:44,605
He thinks we are like Candar and Germiyan...

265
00:24:44,926 --> 00:24:47,325
...who he made kneel and bow, my Shahzade.

266
00:24:47,406 --> 00:24:49,845
But he doesn't know.

267
00:24:49,966 --> 00:24:53,365
We vowed to spread...

268
00:24:53,726 --> 00:24:56,085
...the ideal of Turks in the world.

269
00:24:56,286 --> 00:24:58,605
What can death even do to us?

270
00:25:00,166 --> 00:25:02,725
Do whatever you can, dastard.

271
00:25:09,966 --> 00:25:12,605
I will destroy your culture.

272
00:25:13,486 --> 00:25:15,965
I will crush your ideals!

273
00:25:17,166 --> 00:25:18,925
Osman will fall...

274
00:25:19,886 --> 00:25:22,365
...and you will vanish.

275
00:25:22,806 --> 00:25:23,325
Then...

276
00:25:24,246 --> 00:25:27,725
...he will bow before me like a dog.

277
00:25:28,726 --> 00:25:30,325
Untie him.

278
00:25:32,246 --> 00:25:36,685
Let's see if his feet are
as strong as his tongue.

279
00:25:44,166 --> 00:25:47,405
My Shahzade... My Shahzade!

280
00:25:51,806 --> 00:25:53,725
You dastards.

281
00:25:54,326 --> 00:25:55,605
You dastards!

282
00:25:55,846 --> 00:25:58,885
Fight like a man! My Shahzade!

283
00:26:01,286 --> 00:26:03,285
You will die slowly, Orhan.

284
00:26:03,806 --> 00:26:06,125
My nokers(Mongolian Soldier) will have a feast.

285
00:26:06,446 --> 00:26:10,485
They will stand against you and drink kimiz.

286
00:26:13,206 --> 00:26:14,514
Get him up.

287
00:26:14,526 --> 00:26:18,485
I bear witness that
there is no god but Allah...

288
00:26:34,806 --> 00:26:37,085
You won't die right away.

289
00:26:38,966 --> 00:26:41,645
Pour the oil.

290
00:26:45,046 --> 00:26:49,605
You dastards! You dogs!

291
00:26:51,566 --> 00:26:53,685
I will pour that oil on you as well.

292
00:26:54,366 --> 00:26:55,725
Wait...

293
00:26:57,596 --> 00:26:59,245
Kiliz!

294
00:27:22,166 --> 00:27:30,365
I bear witness that there is no deity but, Allah,
and I bear witness that Muhammad is th...

295
00:27:45,766 --> 00:27:50,045
You will pay the price
of this slap heavily, Bala.

296
00:27:50,366 --> 00:27:51,845
I swear...

297
00:27:51,846 --> 00:27:54,205
You'll wish you were dead!

298
00:27:55,886 --> 00:27:58,565
You too, Gonca. You too.

299
00:27:59,646 --> 00:28:02,925
I did a favour to you, I protected you!

300
00:28:02,966 --> 00:28:05,005
But you let me down!

301
00:28:05,406 --> 00:28:08,005
And you thought I brought the poison, huh?

302
00:28:23,046 --> 00:28:24,565
Ilbay...

303
00:28:25,966 --> 00:28:28,805
I went to the well... Here, drink clean water.

304
00:28:29,406 --> 00:28:30,845
Thank you.

305
00:28:37,006 --> 00:28:38,965
Ayse was not poisoned...

306
00:28:39,766 --> 00:28:41,365
I was also not poisoned...

307
00:28:42,126 --> 00:28:44,125
Did you know it?

308
00:28:48,366 --> 00:28:50,725
Ilbay, did you know about the poison?

309
00:28:53,406 --> 00:28:55,565
Begum is blinded by her ambition.

310
00:28:56,446 --> 00:28:58,445
We need to take measures.

311
00:28:59,166 --> 00:29:02,965
She won't be able to hurt us a bit.

312
00:29:10,406 --> 00:29:11,485
Mother...

313
00:29:12,886 --> 00:29:16,405
Mother, are you alright? You don't seem alright.
-I am alright.

314
00:29:16,526 --> 00:29:17,765
I am alright.

315
00:29:18,446 --> 00:29:19,965
Are you alright?

316
00:29:21,886 --> 00:29:28,205
Did you visit a healer?
-A healer?

317
00:29:30,326 --> 00:29:32,085
Something is different...

318
00:29:33,686 --> 00:29:34,845
Mother...

319
00:29:36,686 --> 00:29:39,725
I wanted to tell this to Orhan first, but...

320
00:29:45,326 --> 00:29:46,925
...I am pregnant.

321
00:29:53,646 --> 00:29:54,805
My daughter...

322
00:29:59,526 --> 00:30:05,005
After all these problems... May it be blessed.

323
00:30:05,726 --> 00:30:07,285
Thanks to Allah..

324
00:30:08,126 --> 00:30:09,685
Thanks to Allah..

325
00:30:13,366 --> 00:30:17,125
May Allah let it grow up
with its father and mother.

326
00:30:22,046 --> 00:30:23,085
Mother...

327
00:30:24,246 --> 00:30:25,965
Orhan will come back, right?

328
00:30:29,726 --> 00:30:32,205
God willing, he will come back, my daughter.

329
00:30:32,366 --> 00:30:33,845
He will come back.

330
00:30:36,166 --> 00:30:40,445
-God willing.
-God willing...

331
00:30:41,646 --> 00:30:44,125
...you will have the baby safe and sound...

332
00:30:44,446 --> 00:30:47,205
...with Orhan Bey, Holofira.

333
00:30:54,966 --> 00:30:57,725
Hug now, huh?

334
00:30:58,806 --> 00:31:00,605
What did I tell you?

335
00:31:01,046 --> 00:31:03,965
You are the mountains behind my sons.

336
00:31:04,486 --> 00:31:07,085
You cannot be separated.

337
00:31:12,726 --> 00:31:14,805
Come on, my daughters.

338
00:31:15,206 --> 00:31:16,245
Come on.

339
00:31:31,686 --> 00:31:34,245
Osman Bey is here. -Orhan!

340
00:31:34,246 --> 00:31:36,125
Come on... Come on..

341
00:32:26,646 --> 00:32:30,245
Osman Bey... My child..

342
00:32:49,086 --> 00:32:52,125
She has a high temperature. Give her to me...

343
00:32:53,166 --> 00:32:56,125
Come here, my dear.

344
00:33:30,446 --> 00:33:33,885
My Bey... Don't go in. The
people inside are not well.

345
00:33:33,886 --> 00:33:36,725
Please find a cure.

346
00:33:42,806 --> 00:33:43,885
My Bey...

347
00:33:45,086 --> 00:33:46,725
Find a cure.

348
00:33:48,126 --> 00:33:49,885
For Allah's sake save us.

349
00:33:49,926 --> 00:33:51,885
Save us from this disease.

350
00:34:09,166 --> 00:34:11,405
Orhan...

351
00:34:22,406 --> 00:34:24,125
Mother...

352
00:34:25,966 --> 00:34:27,485
Orhan is not there!

353
00:34:32,166 --> 00:34:33,085
Mother, Orhan...

354
00:34:33,085 --> 00:34:35,045
Stop, wait, my daughter. Calm down.

355
00:34:35,045 --> 00:34:38,005
Come. Come.

356
00:34:59,206 --> 00:35:02,765
My Bey, are you alright?

357
00:35:03,846 --> 00:35:04,965
I'm alright.

358
00:35:09,126 --> 00:35:12,885
Is there any news from Orhan or Boran?

359
00:35:14,206 --> 00:35:17,045
No. Not yet.

360
00:35:17,886 --> 00:35:19,365
But we'll find them.

361
00:35:30,726 --> 00:35:31,925
Father..

362
00:35:33,486 --> 00:35:35,205
You are not alright.

363
00:35:35,646 --> 00:35:37,245
You have a fever.

364
00:35:38,406 --> 00:35:42,925
Alaeddin... What did you do?
Could you find a way to cure this?

365
00:35:44,646 --> 00:35:46,165
I couldn't, my Bey.

366
00:35:50,206 --> 00:35:52,845
Wherever they brought this disease...

367
00:35:53,926 --> 00:35:56,165
...the effect of the poison is very severe.

368
00:35:56,726 --> 00:36:00,245
But we were able to break its effect a little.

369
00:36:01,246 --> 00:36:03,685
Alps can resist but...

370
00:36:04,926 --> 00:36:07,725
...the elderly and the children cannot, my Bey.

371
00:36:11,086 --> 00:36:12,645
It kills them one by one.

372
00:36:19,006 --> 00:36:20,485
Do your best...

373
00:36:21,286 --> 00:36:23,165
...and find something.

374
00:36:23,206 --> 00:36:25,285
I will try finding a way, father...

375
00:36:29,766 --> 00:36:31,285
Cerkutay Bey.

376
00:36:32,646 --> 00:36:34,965
You know the Mongols.

377
00:36:35,486 --> 00:36:38,085
They won't do something bad to Orhan, right?

378
00:36:38,086 --> 00:36:39,925
They won't kill him, right?

379
00:36:50,006 --> 00:36:52,565
...don't know, Holofira Hatun.

380
00:36:54,526 --> 00:36:55,645
But..

381
00:36:56,046 --> 00:36:59,565
...there is one thing I know. My Shahzade...

382
00:36:59,646 --> 00:37:01,045
...is strong.

383
00:37:01,326 --> 00:37:05,245
My Shahzade is powerful. He won't fall down.

384
00:37:08,366 --> 00:37:09,565
My daughter...

385
00:37:10,166 --> 00:37:11,605
Stand tall.

386
00:37:12,406 --> 00:37:14,245
They cannot do anything to Orhan...

387
00:37:18,006 --> 00:37:23,245
My daughter... my daughter...
-Holofira.. -Bring some water!

388
00:37:24,126 --> 00:37:26,125
What is happening? -Come on!

389
00:37:26,126 --> 00:37:29,325
Take her, she will have
some rest. Come on, take her!

390
00:37:33,766 --> 00:37:35,085
What happened to her?

391
00:37:35,446 --> 00:37:37,325
Among all these bad things...

392
00:37:37,646 --> 00:37:39,205
...hope found us.

393
00:37:41,726 --> 00:37:43,445
Holofira is pregnant.

394
00:37:47,086 --> 00:37:49,285
Orhan will be a father, God willing.

395
00:37:53,606 --> 00:37:55,485
Your state will have a grandchild.

396
00:38:20,526 --> 00:38:22,445
What are you doing here?

397
00:38:24,246 --> 00:38:26,885
I brought you a gift, Ulugan.

398
00:38:39,246 --> 00:38:43,685
A gift for you and
your nokers (Mongolian Soldier).

399
00:38:49,926 --> 00:38:52,525
I did not come here for gold.

400
00:38:53,926 --> 00:38:55,965
I came here to shed blood.

401
00:39:15,926 --> 00:39:18,125
What do you want, Red Hatun?

402
00:39:18,526 --> 00:39:19,805
Just...

403
00:39:22,166 --> 00:39:24,285
I want an antidote for one person.

404
00:39:25,806 --> 00:39:27,445
Don't worry.

405
00:39:28,126 --> 00:39:30,165
Your spy will live.

406
00:39:30,766 --> 00:39:34,605
Osman will bow down to me tomorrow.

407
00:39:34,726 --> 00:39:36,765
And he will take the antidote.

408
00:39:38,606 --> 00:39:40,445
What if the opposite happens?

409
00:39:43,766 --> 00:39:45,285
Then..

410
00:39:47,286 --> 00:39:49,125
..your friend will die.

411
00:39:49,646 --> 00:39:50,805
Ulugan.

412
00:39:51,326 --> 00:39:53,965
You wanted me to give Osman to you.

413
00:39:56,566 --> 00:39:58,485
You cannot stop me.

414
00:40:01,126 --> 00:40:03,685
Thus, we came to you with an agreement.

415
00:40:03,686 --> 00:40:05,845
I never make agreements.

416
00:40:06,926 --> 00:40:09,765
And I punish those who threaten me.

417
00:40:12,086 --> 00:40:14,485
I am not afraid of death, Ulugan.

418
00:40:14,486 --> 00:40:18,125
I will take back the castles that Osman
took from me, one way or another.

419
00:40:18,126 --> 00:40:20,165
Everything Osman has...

420
00:40:20,246 --> 00:40:22,205
...is mine now.

421
00:40:22,846 --> 00:40:26,253
If you draw your sword,
that means we'll be in war.

422
00:40:26,265 --> 00:40:27,405
Gladly.

423
00:40:27,806 --> 00:40:30,365
I will gladly fight against you.

424
00:40:31,486 --> 00:40:35,565
But Osman makes his plans like a wolf.

425
00:40:40,406 --> 00:40:43,645
If you fall, no one will be standing behind you.

426
00:40:44,606 --> 00:40:48,365
The enemies of our enemies are our friends.

427
00:40:49,486 --> 00:40:50,645
Lukas.

428
00:40:55,006 --> 00:40:56,925
Ulugan

429
00:41:02,966 --> 00:41:05,765
We don't want to
be enemies with you.

430
00:41:06,286 --> 00:41:07,525
On the contrary...

431
00:41:09,126 --> 00:41:10,805
..we want to unite..

432
00:41:16,206 --> 00:41:19,335
...and drink kimiz(Turkic-Mongolic drink) together.

433
00:41:32,286 --> 00:41:33,925
I am impressed.

434
00:41:34,406 --> 00:41:35,805
Red Hatun.

435
00:41:43,926 --> 00:41:46,885
If you need help for Osman, we'll be here.

436
00:41:49,206 --> 00:41:51,325
I hope we are on the same side.

437
00:42:18,166 --> 00:42:19,205
Mother...

438
00:42:19,206 --> 00:42:20,845
My daughter.

439
00:42:24,886 --> 00:42:26,765
Father...

440
00:42:26,766 --> 00:42:29,365
Are you here? -I am..

441
00:42:30,086 --> 00:42:31,365
My brother...

442
00:42:35,686 --> 00:42:38,645
Did my brother come with you?

443
00:42:45,206 --> 00:42:46,765
Your brother will come.

444
00:42:49,646 --> 00:42:51,045
He will come.

445
00:42:53,206 --> 00:42:54,605
My brother...

446
00:42:55,246 --> 00:42:57,245
...will come together with his baby...

447
00:42:57,246 --> 00:43:02,245
...right, father? It won't
die this time, right, father?

448
00:43:04,086 --> 00:43:05,725
We will not die, right?

449
00:43:05,726 --> 00:43:10,045
No, my daughter...Don't worry.
Your brother will come back.

450
00:43:10,046 --> 00:43:12,965
We will be a big family again, huh?

451
00:43:14,166 --> 00:43:16,125
We will find the shifa.

452
00:43:18,766 --> 00:43:20,045
Halime...

453
00:43:21,566 --> 00:43:23,285
Halime is gone..

454
00:43:27,806 --> 00:43:29,085
My brother...

455
00:43:29,766 --> 00:43:33,285
If we lose my brother as well..

456
00:43:33,286 --> 00:43:38,285
Look, Halime was little...

457
00:43:38,526 --> 00:43:42,645
Your brother is strong. Nothing will
happen to him. He will come back.

458
00:43:43,126 --> 00:43:44,245
He will come back.

459
00:43:44,246 --> 00:43:47,085
Come on. Have some rest.

460
00:43:53,806 --> 00:43:55,205
Aunt..

461
00:43:55,566 --> 00:43:56,805
Aunt...

462
00:43:58,446 --> 00:44:03,125
Aunt, don't go... It's too cold...

463
00:44:06,966 --> 00:44:08,205
Aunt...

464
00:44:09,126 --> 00:44:11,325
Ah my beautiful daughter...

465
00:44:17,086 --> 00:44:19,125
Her fever did not go down.

466
00:44:30,206 --> 00:44:32,005
What are we going to do?

467
00:44:32,206 --> 00:44:34,925
Our children are burning in front of us.

468
00:44:36,206 --> 00:44:37,925
Does she have an aunt?

469
00:44:38,206 --> 00:44:39,365
She never told me.

470
00:44:39,366 --> 00:44:40,845
I heard it for the first time.

471
00:44:40,846 --> 00:44:42,965
We did not have any
room left in the healing tent.

472
00:44:42,966 --> 00:44:44,485
And we placed her here.

473
00:44:44,486 --> 00:44:46,605
You did well. You did well...

474
00:44:48,286 --> 00:44:49,685
She has...

475
00:44:50,366 --> 00:44:57,205
...something that puts out the fire in my heart.

476
00:44:57,206 --> 00:44:58,765
My Bala, you are not alright.

477
00:44:59,566 --> 00:45:02,885
Come on, have some rest, my Bala.

478
00:45:03,366 --> 00:45:06,565
I'll have some rest, but what about you?

479
00:45:07,086 --> 00:45:09,205
This poison on one side...

480
00:45:09,206 --> 00:45:13,805
...our child Orhan, our
companion Boran on the other...

481
00:45:13,806 --> 00:45:17,845
My Bala, as you, my
people, my tribe feel better...

482
00:45:17,846 --> 00:45:19,805
..I feel better.

483
00:45:19,806 --> 00:45:23,485
Your breath and hearts give me strength.

484
00:45:23,486 --> 00:45:25,245
Come on.

485
00:45:25,886 --> 00:45:28,445
Now you will go and rest.

486
00:45:28,446 --> 00:45:31,445
And you will get up stronger. Come on.

487
00:45:31,446 --> 00:45:33,125
We'll wake up together tomorrow.

488
00:45:33,966 --> 00:45:35,005
Good...

489
00:45:37,646 --> 00:45:40,045
Father...

490
00:45:40,046 --> 00:45:43,685
Father... father don't leave!

491
00:45:45,086 --> 00:45:47,765
It's too dark...

492
00:45:48,246 --> 00:45:50,365
Father, father don't go!

493
00:45:50,366 --> 00:45:52,605
Father...

494
00:45:58,846 --> 00:46:06,645
-It's too dark.
-You're afraid of dark, huh?

495
00:46:08,766 --> 00:46:10,885
But you have a strong heart.

496
00:46:11,806 --> 00:46:15,125
In your eyes, your voice...

497
00:46:16,766 --> 00:46:19,565
...and in your heart,
there is something familiar.

498
00:46:19,926 --> 00:46:22,165
Allah sent you to me to look after.

499
00:46:22,726 --> 00:46:27,045
You joined our table and
ate our food. Don't worry.

500
00:46:27,846 --> 00:46:30,005
Osman Bey is here for you, girl.

501
00:46:31,126 --> 00:46:32,885
Don't worry.

502
00:46:42,326 --> 00:46:43,365
Osman.

503
00:46:44,606 --> 00:46:46,645
Are you alright?

504
00:46:46,966 --> 00:46:49,285
-Alaaddin!
-Mother.

505
00:46:49,406 --> 00:46:52,285
-Don't worry.
-Check him, son. He's not well.

506
00:46:53,206 --> 00:46:56,165
-Are you alright, father?
-It's fine.

507
00:46:56,566 --> 00:46:58,485
You have a high fever.

508
00:47:01,686 --> 00:47:05,405
-I'm fine.
-In the name of Allah.

509
00:47:06,046 --> 00:47:08,805
Father, drink some.

510
00:47:09,166 --> 00:47:10,765
Drink, father.

511
00:47:10,886 --> 00:47:13,245
It will make you feel better.

512
00:47:21,686 --> 00:47:23,445
Take this.

513
00:47:24,366 --> 00:47:25,805
Well...

514
00:47:26,846 --> 00:47:28,565
I need to go now.

515
00:47:29,846 --> 00:47:32,605
Where are you going at this late hour?

516
00:47:34,966 --> 00:47:38,125
There is a star at every dark night, Bala.

517
00:47:38,406 --> 00:47:40,205
It enlightens our way.

518
00:47:40,846 --> 00:47:43,125
I need to find that star.

519
00:47:43,446 --> 00:47:45,525
Don't carry the burden on your own, Osman.

520
00:47:45,766 --> 00:47:48,685
Let me be with you until you find the star.

521
00:47:48,806 --> 00:47:51,805
You're always with me. You stay here.

522
00:47:52,166 --> 00:47:53,685
You stay.

523
00:47:54,046 --> 00:47:56,245
For my nation and state

524
00:47:56,926 --> 00:48:01,325
...I need to find the light myself.

525
00:48:12,566 --> 00:48:16,405
You carry all the burdens of the
state on your shoulders, my Osman.

526
00:48:16,766 --> 00:48:18,805
May Allah help you.

527
00:48:36,886 --> 00:48:38,325
I'm doing...

528
00:48:39,086 --> 00:48:41,285
...everything to take our right, my girl.

529
00:48:41,966 --> 00:48:43,405
Everything.

530
00:48:48,926 --> 00:48:52,085
Sorry for coming inside...

531
00:48:54,486 --> 00:48:56,205
...without permission, Ilbay.

532
00:48:59,166 --> 00:49:01,365
Do you need something, Begum Hatun?

533
00:49:02,006 --> 00:49:03,605
What's the matter?

534
00:49:03,886 --> 00:49:05,765
Not something bad.

535
00:49:06,966 --> 00:49:08,685
Everybody is poisoned.

536
00:49:08,846 --> 00:49:11,085
But somehow, Ayse isn't infected.

537
00:49:11,886 --> 00:49:15,085
So this is all good to me.

538
00:49:17,166 --> 00:49:18,805
Thanks to Allah.

539
00:49:18,966 --> 00:49:21,565
You didn't drink poisonous water, it seems.

540
00:49:22,646 --> 00:49:24,805
Thanks to you, Ilbay.

541
00:49:27,046 --> 00:49:30,085
But I want to know something.

542
00:49:31,406 --> 00:49:37,405
You are Ilbay, grandson of
Sungur Tegin from Kayi bloodline.

543
00:49:39,366 --> 00:49:46,885
Why did you poison your uncle's
son Osman's tribe and family?

544
00:49:49,686 --> 00:49:54,365
No. You're poisoned Begum Hatun.

545
00:49:55,166 --> 00:49:58,445
-You're delusional.
-Stop it, Ilbay.

546
00:49:58,606 --> 00:49:59,965
I know everything.

547
00:50:00,166 --> 00:50:03,525
I heard you talking to Ayse.

548
00:50:03,886 --> 00:50:08,525
What will happen to you when
I tell Osman Bey what I know?

549
00:50:09,046 --> 00:50:10,925
Can you imagine that?

550
00:50:12,446 --> 00:50:14,605
Why would they believe you?

551
00:50:43,406 --> 00:50:46,405
ULUGAN SECRET PLACE

552
00:50:54,486 --> 00:50:56,365
You're a tough man, Bey's son.

553
00:50:56,566 --> 00:51:00,485
Let's see the limits of your strength.

554
00:51:00,886 --> 00:51:06,485
Do your best, you dog.

555
00:51:06,766 --> 00:51:09,965
Nokers(Mongolian Soldier) , show no mercy!

556
00:51:12,086 --> 00:51:15,365
My Shahzade, hold on! Hold on!

557
00:51:16,686 --> 00:51:21,685
Even if I know it will cost my life, I
will drown you in your blood, dog!

558
00:51:22,206 --> 00:51:24,565
Wait for your turn, you fiery boy.

559
00:51:25,966 --> 00:51:27,845
What I'm going to do to you...

560
00:51:27,966 --> 00:51:31,165
...will make you lose your poor mind.

561
00:51:31,646 --> 00:51:33,725
I'm already mad.

562
00:51:35,326 --> 00:51:37,605
It doesn't matter even if I lose my mind.

563
00:51:37,926 --> 00:51:42,125
I will make your ominous head fall, you dog.

564
00:51:42,406 --> 00:51:44,125
We'll see.

565
00:51:45,846 --> 00:51:48,885
Hold on, my Shahzade. Hold on.

566
00:51:49,326 --> 00:51:52,405
For sure, I'm well trained, Boran Bey.

567
00:51:52,726 --> 00:51:55,285
These jackals are incapable of...

568
00:51:55,646 --> 00:51:58,045
...killing and even tiring me up.

569
00:51:58,926 --> 00:52:00,405
Unable?

570
00:52:00,766 --> 00:52:04,205
-I will show you now!
-Altuga!

571
00:52:19,806 --> 00:52:22,365
Keep your hatred in your heart.

572
00:52:25,366 --> 00:52:28,205
His living body is more valuable.

573
00:52:28,686 --> 00:52:33,405
Yet both your living and
dead body are filthy, Ulugan.

574
00:52:33,646 --> 00:52:36,085
Your life is on the edge of my knife.

575
00:52:36,246 --> 00:52:41,285
If you want your tongue to stay in your
mouth and your head on your shoulders,

576
00:52:41,446 --> 00:52:43,725
...watch your words.

577
00:52:49,046 --> 00:52:51,605
You, untie him.

578
00:52:54,486 --> 00:52:58,925
Go and let Osman know
about his shahzade's situation.

579
00:52:59,286 --> 00:53:03,445
If he kneels, his shahzade will live.

580
00:53:04,006 --> 00:53:06,565
If he makes another mistake

581
00:53:06,886 --> 00:53:09,765
...I will send his bones tomorrow.

582
00:53:12,566 --> 00:53:13,885
Cover his eyes.

583
00:53:14,166 --> 00:53:16,685
We'll take care of you

584
00:53:16,886 --> 00:53:18,965
All of you

585
00:53:19,206 --> 00:53:20,685
My Shahzade, hold on.

586
00:53:21,046 --> 00:53:25,525
We'll come for you. Hold on, my Shahzade!
-Ulugan.

587
00:53:26,726 --> 00:53:28,645
You have hopes in vain.

588
00:53:29,566 --> 00:53:33,685
The arrow you shoot will never hit the target.

589
00:53:38,046 --> 00:53:39,765
I couldn't find out, father.

590
00:53:40,766 --> 00:53:43,245
Whatever I tried didn't work.

591
00:53:44,086 --> 00:53:45,725
I slow it down.

592
00:53:46,206 --> 00:53:50,605
I slow it down but they get
worse again after a while.

593
00:53:53,126 --> 00:53:55,805
If we can't find the antidote

594
00:53:56,326 --> 00:53:58,445
...how long can we survive, son?

595
00:53:58,966 --> 00:54:00,885
Weak ones...

596
00:54:01,246 --> 00:54:02,925
...can't survive, mother.

597
00:54:04,566 --> 00:54:06,205
I don't know.

598
00:54:07,446 --> 00:54:10,765
What will we do, my Bey?
They aren't giving us the antidote.

599
00:54:11,446 --> 00:54:14,365
They'd choke us if they had a chance.

600
00:54:24,606 --> 00:54:26,965
If we surrender

601
00:54:28,166 --> 00:54:30,085
...they'll give the antidote.

602
00:54:30,486 --> 00:54:32,445
Surrender?

603
00:54:32,966 --> 00:54:34,765
They want you, Osman.

604
00:54:35,366 --> 00:54:36,445
No.

605
00:54:36,646 --> 00:54:38,845
We'd rather die than surrender.

606
00:54:39,326 --> 00:54:41,365
If Orhan were here

607
00:54:41,886 --> 00:54:44,085
...he wouldn't want this either, father.

608
00:54:53,886 --> 00:54:55,645
This flag...

609
00:54:56,446 --> 00:54:58,885
This tribe will never surrender.

610
00:54:59,886 --> 00:55:01,205
But...

611
00:55:02,246 --> 00:55:04,165
If people die,

612
00:55:04,486 --> 00:55:06,765
If people die one by one,

613
00:55:08,206 --> 00:55:10,245
...nothing will be left behind.

614
00:55:11,486 --> 00:55:14,445
We sacrificed many lives
for these lands, father.

615
00:55:14,446 --> 00:55:16,605
Again we would. All of us would.

616
00:55:17,366 --> 00:55:18,645
You're right, son.

617
00:55:18,766 --> 00:55:21,445
We sacrificed many lives for these lands.

618
00:55:21,766 --> 00:55:23,365
Of course we would.

619
00:55:24,166 --> 00:55:25,365
But...

620
00:55:27,006 --> 00:55:28,845
Our job...

621
00:55:30,126 --> 00:55:32,285
...is not to die, but make live.

622
00:55:33,926 --> 00:55:36,565
If people are out of breath,

623
00:55:36,766 --> 00:55:38,765
...who will this flag wave for?

624
00:55:41,526 --> 00:55:45,325
If the tribe falls, how will the state rise?

625
00:55:48,646 --> 00:55:50,485
We won't die.

626
00:55:52,046 --> 00:55:53,725
We will make live.

627
00:55:55,926 --> 00:55:57,565
Do I have permission, my Bey?

628
00:55:57,926 --> 00:55:59,565
Come in, Yusuf.

629
00:56:00,926 --> 00:56:03,245
-What's the news?
-My Bey.

630
00:56:03,886 --> 00:56:06,645
Begum Hatun isn't around.

631
00:56:07,206 --> 00:56:09,765
I looked everywhere. Nobody has seen her.

632
00:56:10,206 --> 00:56:13,445
I came here to ask if she had some duty here.

633
00:56:18,846 --> 00:56:21,405
It seems she listened to me.

634
00:56:21,966 --> 00:56:23,245
Bala.

635
00:56:24,606 --> 00:56:28,085
-Do you know?
-I asked her to leave the tribe, my Bey.

636
00:56:29,286 --> 00:56:32,245
A personal matter. I will tell you.

637
00:56:39,966 --> 00:56:42,805
Stop struggling, Begum Hatun.

638
00:56:43,926 --> 00:56:46,005
You forced me to do this.

639
00:56:55,486 --> 00:56:57,445
I won't kill you. Don't be afraid.

640
00:56:59,086 --> 00:57:00,765
I can't kill you.

641
00:57:03,686 --> 00:57:07,725
Well... I can't let you expose me either.

642
00:57:15,686 --> 00:57:18,805
Stop struggling. Nobody can hear you here.

643
00:57:31,646 --> 00:57:34,365
I set the fire. You won't feel cold.

644
00:57:35,086 --> 00:57:36,405
I'm leaving now.

645
00:57:36,486 --> 00:57:40,525
If you calm down by the time I
come back, we will talk nicely.

646
00:57:41,366 --> 00:57:42,925
Maybe we can have a deal, huh?

647
00:58:01,326 --> 00:58:05,725
My Bey, Alaaddin has sent
this. It shall make you feel better.

648
00:58:07,806 --> 00:58:10,205
Bala, you take some too.

649
00:58:10,646 --> 00:58:13,085
You need to regain strength too. Come on.

650
00:58:22,406 --> 00:58:25,205
We have to be strong.

651
00:58:30,126 --> 00:58:32,645
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

652
00:58:37,886 --> 00:58:40,645
Are you angry that I sent Begum away?

653
00:58:41,046 --> 00:58:44,245
No. You well thought. Well...

654
00:58:44,326 --> 00:58:47,925
For unity and order, there shouldn't
be troublemakers in the tribe.

655
00:58:52,446 --> 00:58:54,445
My Orhan's dream..

656
00:58:56,046 --> 00:58:58,045
..has come true.

657
00:58:58,606 --> 00:59:00,405
He's going to be a father.

658
00:59:00,846 --> 00:59:02,645
He doesn't know, though.

659
00:59:03,206 --> 00:59:06,405
Yes, he's going to be a father.

660
00:59:07,326 --> 00:59:10,965
Orhan is a strong boy. He'll
feel the baby. Don't worry.

661
00:59:12,086 --> 00:59:13,845
What have you decided, my Bey?

662
00:59:14,206 --> 00:59:15,925
You didn't say anything.

663
00:59:16,166 --> 00:59:18,765
Alaaddin is working day and night, but...

664
00:59:19,046 --> 00:59:21,725
...it seems he won't be
able to find the antidote.

665
00:59:21,846 --> 00:59:24,925
I don't care about myself or our children...

666
00:59:25,206 --> 00:59:28,405
But my people, my nation...

667
00:59:30,326 --> 00:59:33,525
Their breath is a heavy burden for me, Bala.

668
00:59:35,966 --> 00:59:39,005
And surrender on the other side...

669
00:59:39,846 --> 00:59:41,965
That's too heavy as well.

670
00:59:43,246 --> 00:59:47,485
Just sending you to them?

671
00:59:48,966 --> 00:59:50,805
Don't say that, Osman.

672
00:59:51,046 --> 00:59:53,725
How can I accept that?
-Bala.

673
00:59:55,406 --> 00:59:58,285
You and I have gone through many tests.

674
00:59:58,886 --> 01:00:01,565
We loved each other which was a test.

675
01:00:02,326 --> 01:00:04,685
We loved our children which was a test.

676
01:00:04,806 --> 01:00:07,725
And now our child and nation...

677
01:00:09,366 --> 01:00:11,885
This is the new test. Don't worry.

678
01:00:12,126 --> 01:00:14,645
We'll get over this too together.

679
01:00:20,566 --> 01:00:22,205
Do I have permission, my Bey?

680
01:00:23,166 --> 01:00:24,645
Come in, Cerkutay.

681
01:00:31,126 --> 01:00:32,925
Boran..

682
01:00:35,166 --> 01:00:37,125
My Bey.

683
01:00:37,886 --> 01:00:40,445
Are you alright?

684
01:00:41,686 --> 01:00:45,045
I'm fine, my Bey. Thank Allah.

685
01:00:49,366 --> 01:00:51,085
I'm fine, but...

686
01:00:51,846 --> 01:00:53,205
My Shahzade...

687
01:00:55,806 --> 01:00:58,645
Orhan Bey is in a terrible situation, my Bey.

688
01:01:04,486 --> 01:01:06,165
My Bey.

689
01:01:07,286 --> 01:01:09,885
If we go there to help him in no time,

690
01:01:11,566 --> 01:01:13,685
May Allah forbid this, but...

691
01:01:14,526 --> 01:01:16,325
...they will kill Orhan Bey.

692
01:01:17,206 --> 01:01:19,085
Orhan...

693
01:01:25,446 --> 01:01:27,485
Father.

694
01:01:38,966 --> 01:01:41,205
Take a deep breath, come on.

695
01:01:41,726 --> 01:01:43,125
Come on.

696
01:01:43,766 --> 01:01:46,205
I've been fighting for years.

697
01:01:46,566 --> 01:01:48,325
I got many wounds.

698
01:01:48,806 --> 01:01:54,765
But I have never seen such a vile and evil plan.

699
01:01:54,966 --> 01:01:56,965
My Allah.

700
01:01:58,086 --> 01:02:00,525
My Allah, You are the one Who protects.

701
01:02:02,166 --> 01:02:05,125
Don't deprive us of your gifts, my Allah.

702
01:02:05,566 --> 01:02:07,285
Aameen.

703
01:02:11,646 --> 01:02:13,045
My Bey.

704
01:02:13,966 --> 01:02:16,085
The situation is worse than yesterday.

705
01:02:16,286 --> 01:02:18,805
We're losing more lives day by day.

706
01:02:29,326 --> 01:02:30,765
My Bey.

707
01:02:31,846 --> 01:02:33,605
A Mongolian commander is here.

708
01:02:34,246 --> 01:02:35,805
Let him come.

709
01:03:08,886 --> 01:03:11,605
Don't spill out hatred against me.

710
01:03:12,246 --> 01:03:16,485
Who did this to you is your Osman Bey.

711
01:03:17,606 --> 01:03:21,805
You're in this condition because
of his arrogance and impertinence.

712
01:03:23,246 --> 01:03:25,205
What do you say, Osman?

713
01:03:25,566 --> 01:03:27,765
Will you be their death?

714
01:03:27,966 --> 01:03:29,765
Have you made up your mind?

715
01:03:30,366 --> 01:03:32,525
Will you bow and kneel?

716
01:03:40,046 --> 01:03:42,005
You won.

717
01:03:43,575 --> 01:03:44,575
You won.

718
01:03:59,606 --> 01:04:02,125
If you had given a different response

719
01:04:02,686 --> 01:04:05,885
...I wouldn't wait for the
poison to break your people...

720
01:04:06,086 --> 01:04:08,405
...but paint this square with blood.

721
01:04:10,966 --> 01:04:12,405
Now...

722
01:04:13,526 --> 01:04:14,725
Kneel.

723
01:04:15,806 --> 01:04:18,805
I did this only for my innocent people.

724
01:04:20,046 --> 01:04:21,805
Give me the antidote now.

725
01:04:22,646 --> 01:04:26,045
-I said kneel!
-What are you saying?

726
01:04:29,406 --> 01:04:35,325
Wait. Draw back.

727
01:04:54,566 --> 01:04:58,245
I never kneel.

728
01:05:00,686 --> 01:05:03,005
I said you win.

729
01:05:03,926 --> 01:05:06,165
I surrender now.

730
01:05:11,366 --> 01:05:12,965
So be it.

731
01:05:13,206 --> 01:05:15,365
You surrendered, anyway.

732
01:05:15,926 --> 01:05:22,085
In Sogut, you will bow and kneel before me.

733
01:05:23,286 --> 01:05:25,085
Hand out the antidote now.

734
01:05:28,766 --> 01:05:32,605
Take this to every tribe whose well is poisoned.

735
01:05:42,686 --> 01:05:46,725
Your people are mine, after all.

736
01:05:48,126 --> 01:05:50,645
I don't want them to die.

737
01:05:58,366 --> 01:06:02,205
Shahzade Orhan. Where is he?

738
01:06:08,886 --> 01:06:12,845
We'll release him, Osman. Don't worry.

739
01:06:14,526 --> 01:06:18,645
But there is something you need to do first.

740
01:06:19,046 --> 01:06:22,925
You will visit every land of yours with me.

741
01:06:24,206 --> 01:06:29,245
And tell your people that you
bowed against Mongolians.

742
01:06:41,486 --> 01:06:43,725
Come on! Chain his hands!

743
01:06:43,726 --> 01:06:46,805
Don't touch me!

744
01:06:49,166 --> 01:06:51,085
-Boran..
My Bey...

745
01:06:57,286 --> 01:06:58,685
Make them move.

746
01:07:00,086 --> 01:07:03,045
Father... no! -Father!

747
01:07:03,046 --> 01:07:08,805
Father, no! -Father!

748
01:07:09,686 --> 01:07:11,125
My Alaeddin Bey!

749
01:07:11,126 --> 01:07:14,925
Father! -No! No!

750
01:07:15,766 --> 01:07:23,165
Father, what are you doing? Don't!

751
01:07:24,966 --> 01:07:27,765
Don't!

752
01:07:28,566 --> 01:07:38,405
Father, what are you doing? Don't!
-Stop! Stop!

753
01:07:41,966 --> 01:07:47,445
Father! Father!

754
01:07:47,446 --> 01:07:51,885
Let me go! Let me go!

755
01:07:51,886 --> 01:07:54,245
No, Alaeddin!

756
01:07:54,246 --> 01:07:57,645
Don't!

757
01:07:57,646 --> 01:08:04,845
Don't! Father! Father!

758
01:08:04,846 --> 01:08:07,325
Don't!

759
01:08:07,326 --> 01:08:09,565
Let me go!

760
01:08:19,765 --> 01:08:25,805
The boots.

761
01:08:29,606 --> 01:08:33,005
Mother, let me go!
-Alaeddin stop! Stop!

762
01:08:33,006 --> 01:08:34,125
Let me go!

763
01:08:34,126 --> 01:08:39,925
Let me go! -Father! Dastard dog!

764
01:08:39,926 --> 01:08:41,925
I will kill you all!

765
01:08:49,006 --> 01:08:53,645
Alaeddin stop! Stop!

766
01:08:55,966 --> 01:09:02,444
Don't take our Bey!

767
01:09:23,286 --> 01:09:26,564
Don't leave us!

768
01:09:26,685 --> 01:09:29,245
You are trying for no reason, you Altuga dog.

769
01:09:30,286 --> 01:09:35,404
Your torture will only make me stronger.

770
01:09:35,926 --> 01:09:38,205
It will strengthen my faith, you dog.

771
01:09:42,845 --> 01:09:44,205
I heard..

772
01:09:44,725 --> 01:09:47,125
..these words in Samarkand..

773
01:09:47,126 --> 01:09:48,765
...Konya...

774
01:09:49,566 --> 01:09:52,045
...and other Turk lands, Bey's son.

775
01:09:54,566 --> 01:09:56,165
Ask this steel.

776
01:09:56,846 --> 01:09:58,165
What do you say, steel?

777
01:10:03,486 --> 01:10:05,165
Brave hands..

778
01:10:06,166 --> 01:10:10,605
...were broken one by one before
the strength of Mongols, right?

779
01:10:12,126 --> 01:10:14,005
You will also be broken.

780
01:10:19,566 --> 01:10:21,725
The ropes around your wrists...

781
01:10:21,726 --> 01:10:24,645
...will be the halter of your valiants.

782
01:10:25,926 --> 01:10:27,925
With these blazing irons...

783
01:10:29,406 --> 01:10:33,085
...I will strip the skin off the bones of many.

784
01:10:37,446 --> 01:10:39,085
If martyrdom...

785
01:10:39,126 --> 01:10:41,405
...is written in the fate of my valiants...

786
01:10:41,486 --> 01:10:43,525
...they will gladly embrace it.

787
01:10:44,406 --> 01:10:46,205
One of us might die...

788
01:10:46,326 --> 01:10:48,325
...but a thousand will come after him.

789
01:10:48,326 --> 01:10:50,045
For every one of us who falls..

790
01:10:50,286 --> 01:10:53,285
...a thousand will rise.

791
01:10:53,286 --> 01:10:55,165
But your evilness..

792
01:10:55,686 --> 01:10:58,965
...before that evillness of
yours take root in this land...

793
01:10:59,286 --> 01:11:01,885
...your miserable head will be cut off.

794
01:11:02,966 --> 01:11:05,485
Orhan, Orhan.

795
01:11:05,606 --> 01:11:10,045
Even your father Osman became the dog of Ulugan.

796
01:11:10,526 --> 01:11:11,645
Tell me.

797
01:11:12,246 --> 01:11:14,405
Who will cut my head off now?

798
01:11:14,766 --> 01:11:17,525
Even if the Turk is chained, he is still a wolf.

799
01:11:18,006 --> 01:11:20,725
Don't you feel victorious.

800
01:11:21,006 --> 01:11:23,125
There are many valiants...

801
01:11:23,326 --> 01:11:25,805
...who can take your dirty head...

802
01:11:25,926 --> 01:11:28,325
..in our lands.

803
01:11:28,446 --> 01:11:31,405
I will bury those valiants
that you think is many...

804
01:11:31,406 --> 01:11:33,805
...in a single grave, Orhan.

805
01:11:34,886 --> 01:11:36,685
Kayi's dark fate...

806
01:11:36,766 --> 01:11:39,725
...was written when you
let Cerkutay in the tribe...

807
01:11:39,726 --> 01:11:42,205
...who carried Mongol blood.

808
01:11:44,206 --> 01:11:46,885
Now I understand your desire for revenge.

809
01:11:47,446 --> 01:11:49,885
You are mad because Cerkutay chose us...

810
01:11:50,566 --> 01:11:52,805
..and not you.

811
01:11:53,806 --> 01:11:56,405
That's why your heart is in pain.

812
01:11:56,766 --> 01:11:58,285
But, dog...

813
01:11:58,606 --> 01:12:01,005
..you will burn in flames.

814
01:12:01,006 --> 01:12:04,165
There is only one fire that burns in me, Orhan.

815
01:12:04,486 --> 01:12:06,205
The fire of revenge.

816
01:12:08,046 --> 01:12:10,645
That dastard will be crushed under the...

817
01:12:10,646 --> 01:12:13,245
...shoes of my horse like a traitor and die.

818
01:12:14,006 --> 01:12:18,005
The world will see the power of Mongols.

819
01:12:18,006 --> 01:12:22,005
Kayis, Byzantium, all of you.

820
01:12:22,606 --> 01:12:25,685
Everyone will bow down to Mongols.

821
01:12:43,446 --> 01:12:47,085
I know how precious Poena is to you.

822
01:12:47,086 --> 01:12:49,205
But aren't you exaggerating a bit?

823
01:12:50,846 --> 01:12:54,005
You got us into a fight with that dirty Mongol.

824
01:12:54,686 --> 01:12:57,965
I gave years of my life to Poena, Lukas.

825
01:12:58,766 --> 01:13:02,685
And now, when I had
Osman and Bala in my hands...

826
01:13:03,766 --> 01:13:05,605
That damned Mongol...

827
01:13:08,646 --> 01:13:10,405
...ruined all my plans.

828
01:13:10,406 --> 01:13:14,285
Are you angry with Ulugan
because he ruined your plans or...

829
01:13:17,366 --> 01:13:20,045
...because he tried to kill Poena?

830
01:13:30,886 --> 01:13:33,205
What are you trying to say, Lukas?

831
01:13:38,566 --> 01:13:44,445
After Poena ends the Kayis, it will be her turn.

832
01:13:45,006 --> 01:13:46,605
You know that, right?

833
01:13:47,926 --> 01:13:51,725
We cannot let a single Kayi live.

834
01:13:52,966 --> 01:13:55,045
Even if it's Poena.

835
01:13:59,406 --> 01:14:01,285
Sure.

836
01:14:04,886 --> 01:14:06,685
Don't worry.

837
01:14:14,126 --> 01:14:17,605
Sir, Ulugan went to Kayi tribe.

838
01:14:17,966 --> 01:14:21,163
Osman took the antidote
and surrendered to Ulugan.

839
01:14:21,175 --> 01:14:22,245
Good.

840
01:14:22,526 --> 01:14:24,285
This is good news, Hristo.

841
01:14:24,286 --> 01:14:25,525
Gather our army.

842
01:14:25,526 --> 01:14:27,245
They must be ready.

843
01:14:29,166 --> 01:14:38,405
Once Osman falls, we will start from the
borders and take back what is ours, one by one.

844
01:14:40,406 --> 01:14:42,605
Lukas, you heard Ulugan.

845
01:14:43,566 --> 01:14:49,845
Attacking Osman's lands and
making him your enemy is not wise.

846
01:14:50,286 --> 01:14:54,245
Once Osman falls, none
of it will matter anymore.

847
01:14:55,286 --> 01:14:58,125
They will think we are their friends.

848
01:14:58,566 --> 01:15:03,525
But I won't let them keep what is mine, Sofia.

849
01:15:13,166 --> 01:15:15,245
This is the result of his arrogance.

850
01:15:15,286 --> 01:15:17,645
You see the situation of your leader?

851
01:15:18,046 --> 01:15:20,365
Look at him, so you'll learn a lesson.

852
01:15:28,686 --> 01:15:31,565
My Bey...

853
01:15:33,206 --> 01:15:35,805
Father..

854
01:15:38,846 --> 01:15:40,805
I wish my Allah had taken my life..

855
01:15:41,286 --> 01:15:44,525
..so that I wouldn't have to
see my Bey in this state, brother.

856
01:15:44,526 --> 01:15:46,885
I cannot draw my sword..

857
01:15:47,806 --> 01:15:50,485
...and this shame will not leave me forever.

858
01:15:52,486 --> 01:15:57,285
Mother... Mother, we won't let
them take my father, right, mother?

859
01:15:57,286 --> 01:16:00,325
Fatma, your father is doing
everything for our people.

860
01:16:00,486 --> 01:16:02,165
Stand tall, my daughter.

861
01:16:03,166 --> 01:16:04,405
Stand tall.

862
01:16:05,206 --> 01:16:07,285
As I promised, Osman.

863
01:16:07,886 --> 01:16:11,005
Everyone in your tribe is healthy again.

864
01:16:12,086 --> 01:16:17,445
When the antidote reaches them, everyone in
all your lands will be in the same condition.

865
01:16:19,046 --> 01:16:23,805
But this is the end of your state.

866
01:16:29,606 --> 01:16:35,005
As long as their traditions live, a
Turk will never be left without a state.

867
01:16:36,646 --> 01:16:41,045
But we could not teach this to those like you.

868
01:16:41,166 --> 01:16:43,765
I will destroy your traditions as well.

869
01:16:43,766 --> 01:16:51,765
I will make your descendants forget everything
you believe and sacrifice your lives for.

870
01:16:53,166 --> 01:16:56,645
Father! Father!

871
01:16:57,126 --> 01:17:01,005
Father!

872
01:17:01,006 --> 01:17:03,285
Nokers(Mongolian Soldier) will stay in your tribe.

873
01:17:04,606 --> 01:17:09,925
As long as no one causes
trouble, no one's life will be taken.

874
01:17:11,326 --> 01:17:12,685
Come on now.

875
01:17:12,726 --> 01:17:15,125
No!

876
01:17:27,246 --> 01:17:29,725
Father!

877
01:18:09,286 --> 01:18:12,325
My Allah, protect us.

878
01:19:17,046 --> 01:19:20,125
Don't worry.

879
01:19:20,966 --> 01:19:24,965
For sure, they cannot do anything to us!

880
01:19:29,766 --> 01:19:31,525
Move!

881
01:19:34,926 --> 01:19:37,165
Drop it!

882
01:19:37,166 --> 01:19:40,725
Move! Move!

883
01:19:45,406 --> 01:19:47,805
Shut up!

884
01:20:11,886 --> 01:20:15,805
Don't touch my father!

885
01:20:35,926 --> 01:20:39,405
What are you doing?!

886
01:20:49,526 --> 01:20:51,525
Don't touch it!

887
01:20:54,326 --> 01:20:58,645
Don't touch our banner!

888
01:21:07,126 --> 01:21:09,965
Our banner!

889
01:21:14,406 --> 01:21:18,165
Dastard dogs! Dastard dogs!

890
01:23:34,846 --> 01:23:37,565
What did you do to Osman Bey?

891
01:23:51,286 --> 01:23:55,525
Don't hurt the people!

892
01:23:57,046 --> 01:23:59,165
Why do you hurt innocent people?

893
01:23:59,166 --> 01:24:02,565
Don't touch them!

894
01:24:02,566 --> 01:24:08,365
Come! Look at your Bey's face! Come!

895
01:24:08,366 --> 01:24:09,925
Look at Osman Bey!

896
01:24:09,926 --> 01:24:11,405
Open your eyes! Look at him!

897
01:24:11,406 --> 01:24:13,205
Look at your Osman Bey!

898
01:24:13,486 --> 01:24:14,485
Don't touch them!

899
01:24:14,486 --> 01:24:16,885
What do you want from innocent people?

900
01:24:16,966 --> 01:24:20,925
Dastard dog! What do you
want from them? My dear...

901
01:24:20,926 --> 01:24:22,005
Don't worry.

902
01:24:22,006 --> 01:24:25,205
It will be alright.

903
01:24:25,206 --> 01:24:26,645
Don't hurt innocent people!

904
01:24:26,646 --> 01:24:29,165
Look at your Bey!

905
01:24:29,166 --> 01:24:32,285
He is in this situation because
of his ambition and courage!

906
01:24:32,326 --> 01:24:35,485
And you are in this situation
because of his ambition!

907
01:24:35,566 --> 01:24:38,005
You are suffering from diseases.

908
01:24:38,126 --> 01:24:40,525
You have a miserable Bey!

909
01:24:41,046 --> 01:24:44,725
Don't worry...

910
01:24:45,206 --> 01:24:48,045
I will break free from these chains.

911
01:24:49,126 --> 01:24:53,645
Ulugan... Then you will stand before me.

912
01:24:54,086 --> 01:24:56,085
Then we will see..

913
01:24:56,086 --> 01:24:59,405
...if you will get away with this oppression...

914
01:24:59,406 --> 01:25:01,125
Hang on.

915
01:25:05,926 --> 01:25:09,685
Don't touch the banner! No!

916
01:25:09,686 --> 01:25:11,605
No!

917
01:25:23,126 --> 01:25:25,885
O people! Don't worry!

918
01:25:25,886 --> 01:25:29,965
For sure, these days will pass! Allah
is with us, we will not give up hope!

919
01:26:20,766 --> 01:26:22,005
Stop...

920
01:26:22,566 --> 01:26:23,925
Stop...

921
01:26:24,326 --> 01:26:25,525
Stop!

922
01:26:32,686 --> 01:26:34,285
What happened Osman?

923
01:26:35,006 --> 01:26:37,005
I have to pray.

924
01:26:37,006 --> 01:26:39,325
It's time for prayer.

925
01:27:11,006 --> 01:27:12,245
My Bey...

926
01:27:13,246 --> 01:27:16,765
Shall we lay a hide on
the ground for you as well?

927
01:27:19,926 --> 01:27:21,485
Don't worry...

928
01:27:22,526 --> 01:27:24,325
When we arrive in Sogut...

929
01:27:24,406 --> 01:27:26,645
...you will worship me...

930
01:27:26,646 --> 01:27:28,885
...in front of your people.

931
01:27:31,526 --> 01:27:34,885
From now on, you will
direct all your prayers to me.

932
01:27:36,486 --> 01:27:38,245
I decide..

933
01:27:39,846 --> 01:27:41,685
..if you die or live.

934
01:27:42,446 --> 01:27:44,245
I am the one who is victorious.

935
01:27:44,306 --> 01:27:46,925
There is no Victor except Allah.

936
01:27:52,126 --> 01:27:56,645
I bow to no one except Allah.

937
01:28:21,366 --> 01:28:23,445
Allah is the greatest!

938
01:29:10,406 --> 01:29:12,765
I thought you had calmed down.

939
01:29:13,086 --> 01:29:14,645
But you didn't.

940
01:29:27,566 --> 01:29:29,325
I will open your mouth.

941
01:29:29,846 --> 01:29:31,605
But don't yell.

942
01:29:32,326 --> 01:29:34,325
We need to talk.

943
01:29:37,046 --> 01:29:39,045
Talk about what?

944
01:29:39,606 --> 01:29:42,885
You think I will forget what you did to me?
-Look.

945
01:29:43,926 --> 01:29:46,045
Say thanks first.

946
01:29:46,726 --> 01:29:48,845
You seemed to have manners.

947
01:29:49,806 --> 01:29:52,965
Aren't you afraid that this
will be heard by people?

948
01:29:53,126 --> 01:29:54,805
Afraid of whom?

949
01:29:55,646 --> 01:29:57,405
Osman?

950
01:29:58,086 --> 01:30:00,165
Osman's finished, Begum Hatun.

951
01:30:02,446 --> 01:30:05,565
Mongolians got him. The tribe has no head.

952
01:30:06,526 --> 01:30:08,565
My time has come.

953
01:30:09,566 --> 01:30:12,805
The reign of Ilbay Bey,
grandson of Sungur Tegin.

954
01:30:13,966 --> 01:30:17,605
What did Osman Bey do
to you and you're so hateful?

955
01:30:17,726 --> 01:30:19,245
What did he do?

956
01:30:19,366 --> 01:30:22,605
By making use of my
grandfather Sungur Tegin's legacy,

957
01:30:23,046 --> 01:30:25,485
...he established a state for himself.

958
01:30:25,966 --> 01:30:28,925
Now I will take back the
legacy that was my right.

959
01:30:29,326 --> 01:30:30,770
What do you want from me?

960
01:30:30,782 --> 01:30:32,405
You should know this first.

961
01:30:33,446 --> 01:30:34,885
I won't harm you.

962
01:30:35,166 --> 01:30:37,525
Until I sit on the chair

963
01:30:38,206 --> 01:30:41,805
...I will do my best to stop you
from telling the others what you know.

964
01:30:42,246 --> 01:30:44,045
You will wait here.

965
01:30:44,766 --> 01:30:47,565
-Then what?
-You will stand beside me.

966
01:30:48,206 --> 01:30:49,565
Maybe.

967
01:30:50,166 --> 01:30:51,885
Always.

968
01:30:54,566 --> 01:30:56,005
We can get married.

969
01:30:56,366 --> 01:30:57,285
No?

970
01:31:00,326 --> 01:31:04,565
You think I will say yes just
because you have the chair?

971
01:31:04,926 --> 01:31:08,565
You will, Begum Hatun. You will.

972
01:31:09,486 --> 01:31:12,245
The ambition and desire for power...

973
01:31:13,166 --> 01:31:16,005
...in your beautiful eyes
will make you say that.

974
01:31:20,086 --> 01:31:22,965
Don't be stubborn now. You must be hungry.

975
01:31:46,006 --> 01:31:48,045
Nobody can hold me by force!

976
01:31:53,006 --> 01:31:56,605
Although you're blinded by your
anger, you are a smart woman.

977
01:31:56,886 --> 01:31:58,925
And also strong.

978
01:32:22,326 --> 01:32:24,685
You and I won't rule only the frontiers...

979
01:32:26,806 --> 01:32:28,965
...but the whole world, Begum Hatun.

980
01:32:54,406 --> 01:32:57,325
Osman Bey! Osman Bey!

981
01:32:59,046 --> 01:33:02,125
Release my Bey, dastards!

982
01:33:07,886 --> 01:33:10,245
O people of Sogut!

983
01:33:10,526 --> 01:33:12,405
Don't be worrying.

984
01:33:12,686 --> 01:33:14,805
For sure, we will be alright.

985
01:33:15,206 --> 01:33:17,045
Untie him and get him down.

986
01:33:17,406 --> 01:33:19,365
Release Osman Bey!

987
01:33:29,286 --> 01:33:31,925
Osman Bey!

988
01:33:35,846 --> 01:33:37,565
My Bey!

989
01:33:52,566 --> 01:33:54,645
Release Osman Bey!

990
01:34:06,766 --> 01:34:08,765
Osman, stand up.

991
01:34:09,166 --> 01:34:11,725
Leave him.

992
01:34:12,926 --> 01:34:15,405
You disbeliever dog!

993
01:34:15,726 --> 01:34:17,885
What have they done to you, my Bey.

994
01:34:19,246 --> 01:34:20,885
My boy.

995
01:34:22,166 --> 01:34:24,125
My boy.

996
01:34:24,526 --> 01:34:26,205
-Are you alright.
-I'm fine.

997
01:34:26,286 --> 01:34:28,165
Don't worry.

998
01:34:28,886 --> 01:34:30,405
We'll be good.

999
01:34:31,326 --> 01:34:33,685
We'll be good. All good.

1000
01:34:33,926 --> 01:34:35,645
Go to your mother now.

1001
01:34:35,846 --> 01:34:39,645
Come on.
Let me kiss you.

1002
01:34:54,326 --> 01:34:57,125
You devil's dog.

1003
01:34:57,926 --> 01:35:00,365
Get your hands off!

1004
01:35:05,086 --> 01:35:10,605
The courage that child takes from your eyes...

1005
01:35:12,006 --> 01:35:15,725
There will be sign of it soon.

1006
01:35:16,406 --> 01:35:21,005
You will fall off even that child's eyes.

1007
01:35:21,886 --> 01:35:26,965
In the hearts of those
children, there is endless faith.

1008
01:35:27,006 --> 01:35:33,325
It's the faith that will
destroy people like you.

1009
01:35:34,526 --> 01:35:36,325
Walk like this...

1010
01:35:37,206 --> 01:35:41,885
...before your people
in the streets of this city.

1011
01:35:42,206 --> 01:35:46,925
Then we will see if they have
any faith left in their hearts.

1012
01:35:48,246 --> 01:35:50,085
Take him.

1013
01:35:53,126 --> 01:35:55,205
Release Osman Bey!

1014
01:35:57,966 --> 01:36:00,245
Release Osman Bey!

1015
01:36:03,326 --> 01:36:05,205
Don't worry!

1016
01:36:07,086 --> 01:36:09,005
O people

1017
01:36:09,206 --> 01:36:13,285
We won't give up! We won't collapse!

1018
01:36:13,526 --> 01:36:16,925
Where are they taking you, my Bey?
-We won't give up.

1019
01:36:17,166 --> 01:36:21,765
Don't worry! Stop harming people!

1020
01:36:21,846 --> 01:36:26,405
Don't harm people!
Don't worry, my people!

1021
01:36:30,166 --> 01:36:35,485
Allah's willing! Allah's willing!
Allah's willing!

1022
01:36:36,846 --> 01:36:39,205
Don't worry.

1023
01:36:43,806 --> 01:36:46,365
O people of Sogut!

1024
01:36:46,486 --> 01:36:49,045
Our state will never collapse!

1025
01:36:49,566 --> 01:36:55,005
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1026
01:36:58,046 --> 01:37:02,685
You're done, Orhan. You
will take your last breath now.

1027
01:37:08,646 --> 01:37:11,805
Commander Ulugan got Osman, Altuga.

1028
01:37:13,686 --> 01:37:17,085
-My Bey...
Did you hear, Orhan?

1029
01:37:17,526 --> 01:37:21,645
Your father knelt before us. But he's too late.

1030
01:37:22,086 --> 01:37:24,685
You're out of life.

1031
01:37:25,286 --> 01:37:29,565
We will throw your dead
body at your father's feet.

1032
01:37:29,926 --> 01:37:38,685
One day... You will pay for what you did.

1033
01:37:40,446 --> 01:37:42,685
One day.

1034
01:37:44,966 --> 01:37:48,925
Nobody can beat us, Orhan.

1035
01:37:49,406 --> 01:37:52,565
It's time for you to die.

1036
01:38:02,406 --> 01:38:04,325
I'm here, brother!

1037
01:38:13,886 --> 01:38:18,605
-Alps, attack!
-I'm here for you, brother.

1038
01:38:19,006 --> 01:38:21,605
Come here!

1039
01:38:26,366 --> 01:38:28,645
I'm here, brother!

1040
01:38:36,766 --> 01:38:38,845
I'm here, brother.

1041
01:38:39,686 --> 01:38:43,125
What have they done to you, brother?

1042
01:38:44,006 --> 01:38:48,925
Nobody can harm me as long
as I have a brother like you.

1043
01:38:51,486 --> 01:38:53,085
Alaaddin.

1044
01:39:17,926 --> 01:39:20,165
-Altuga.
-Yes, Altuga.

1045
01:39:20,206 --> 01:39:22,565
I will be your death, brother.

1046
01:39:22,926 --> 01:39:25,525
Now you will use your weapons..

1047
01:39:25,766 --> 01:39:30,765
...and end your life that you
have led like a traitor. Come on!

1048
01:39:44,726 --> 01:39:46,565
You were like this before too.

1049
01:39:46,646 --> 01:39:50,405
If Balgay hadn't taken you with
him, you'd have lived like a coward.

1050
01:39:50,406 --> 01:39:52,725
You were always weak, brother.

1051
01:39:53,366 --> 01:39:55,845
You're still weak. Come on.

1052
01:39:56,126 --> 01:39:58,285
Come on, attack me.

1053
01:40:08,966 --> 01:40:11,805
Don't make me kill my own brother, Altuga.

1054
01:40:11,846 --> 01:40:13,805
Yours isn't the right path.

1055
01:40:13,966 --> 01:40:15,405
Leave that path.

1056
01:40:15,606 --> 01:40:20,045
I'd rather die than be a
traitor of Mongolians like you.

1057
01:40:21,486 --> 01:40:25,845
Alaaddin, how are the people in our tribe doing?

1058
01:40:25,966 --> 01:40:29,165
I will tell you, brother.

1059
01:40:31,206 --> 01:40:35,005
I will tell you something.

1060
01:40:37,126 --> 01:40:39,205
Come, come.

1061
01:40:39,366 --> 01:40:42,845
Alaaddin, bad news or good news?

1062
01:40:42,926 --> 01:40:45,365
Come on, brother.

1063
01:40:46,766 --> 01:40:48,245
It's good news.

1064
01:40:48,246 --> 01:40:50,125
You'll see when you go there.

1065
01:40:50,166 --> 01:40:52,205
Behind you, Alaaddin!

1066
01:40:58,526 --> 01:41:02,205
Let's go, brother! My brave brother!

1067
01:41:02,366 --> 01:41:04,085
Let's go.

1068
01:41:09,646 --> 01:41:11,565
Brother!

1069
01:41:23,926 --> 01:41:25,845
The worst day of Kayis!

1070
01:41:26,046 --> 01:41:28,925
-See, Osman?
-Stop this cruelty!

1071
01:41:29,126 --> 01:41:31,885
Your people's tears.

1072
01:41:32,206 --> 01:41:34,485
The filth in their hearts...

1073
01:41:34,686 --> 01:41:37,885
...is flowing out due to their respect for you.

1074
01:41:44,766 --> 01:41:47,965
See where arrogance ends up?

1075
01:41:51,526 --> 01:41:57,565
What you call forced respect is the filth.

1076
01:41:57,806 --> 01:42:03,285
You will never know what true respect is.

1077
01:42:06,206 --> 01:42:08,525
You disbeliever dog!

1078
01:42:30,606 --> 01:42:32,645
You're here, huh?

1079
01:42:33,526 --> 01:42:36,845
I didn't want to miss the
show, Commander Ulugan.

1080
01:42:39,646 --> 01:42:42,525
Thanks for the invitation.

1081
01:42:47,006 --> 01:42:53,765
With our power, we again united
all the heathens against us, huh?

1082
01:42:56,446 --> 01:42:58,765
Thank Allah.

1083
01:43:01,126 --> 01:43:02,805
Power, huh?

1084
01:43:03,126 --> 01:43:06,845
You're arrogant even in chains, Osman.

1085
01:43:07,806 --> 01:43:15,085
I'd prefer to kill you myself, but...

1086
01:43:18,686 --> 01:43:21,045
...seeing you like this...

1087
01:43:21,926 --> 01:43:24,125
...is priceless.

1088
01:43:24,726 --> 01:43:28,565
Come, come to me.

1089
01:43:31,246 --> 01:43:33,285
Bring Osman.

1090
01:43:33,686 --> 01:43:36,045
He has things to tell his people.

1091
01:43:38,246 --> 01:43:41,965
Get off your hands!

1092
01:43:43,886 --> 01:43:48,725
-I will...
-Lighten up, Sofia.

1093
01:43:49,206 --> 01:43:52,005
Your little angel is fine.

1094
01:43:53,166 --> 01:43:55,965
Seeing Osman like this...

1095
01:43:57,126 --> 01:44:00,205
We couldn't imagine this much.

1096
01:44:00,726 --> 01:44:04,485
It's not enough that Osman
and Bala will live with this shame.

1097
01:44:04,806 --> 01:44:06,765
If not today, tomorrow.

1098
01:44:07,046 --> 01:44:12,925
If not by Ulugan, they will...

1099
01:44:14,966 --> 01:44:17,365
...be killed by me.

1100
01:44:55,526 --> 01:44:57,725
Allah is the greatest!

1101
01:45:01,326 --> 01:45:05,165
Your nokers (Mongolian Soldier) are dead.
Surrender to Osman Bey's justice.

1102
01:45:05,366 --> 01:45:07,405
Osman Bey, huh?

1103
01:45:09,966 --> 01:45:12,445
You can't give me orders, Cerkutay.

1104
01:45:12,526 --> 01:45:15,765
You can't give me orders. I will never give up.

1105
01:45:15,806 --> 01:45:17,285
Ever!

1106
01:45:29,766 --> 01:45:32,285
We will never die before we wipe you off!

1107
01:45:32,526 --> 01:45:34,805
Allah is the greatest!

1108
01:45:49,886 --> 01:45:52,965
Last warning. Drop your dagger.

1109
01:45:55,166 --> 01:45:57,285
Surrender.

1110
01:45:57,686 --> 01:46:00,165
I never bow, Cerkutay.

1111
01:46:00,246 --> 01:46:03,885
You know me. Never.

1112
01:46:07,526 --> 01:46:10,365
You're still weak, Cerkutay.

1113
01:46:12,006 --> 01:46:13,605
Still.

1114
01:46:24,766 --> 01:46:26,645
Is everyone alright?

1115
01:46:34,846 --> 01:46:37,525
-My Bey..
-Alaeddin...

1116
01:46:37,526 --> 01:46:39,245
Tell me brother.

1117
01:46:39,366 --> 01:46:42,165
How did you find this place?

1118
01:46:42,166 --> 01:46:44,085
How is my father?

1119
01:46:44,366 --> 01:46:45,645
Boran Bey.

1120
01:46:46,006 --> 01:46:47,205
My Shahzade.

1121
01:46:47,206 --> 01:46:49,365
This time we made a big plan.

1122
01:46:49,366 --> 01:46:51,205
I will tell you everything now.

1123
01:46:51,206 --> 01:46:52,925
Now listen to me carefully.

1124
01:46:54,966 --> 01:46:58,525
I will surrender to Ulugan
to save my people from...

1125
01:46:58,846 --> 01:47:00,365
...the poison and the Mongols.

1126
01:47:00,366 --> 01:47:01,645
What are you saying, my Bey?

1127
01:47:01,646 --> 01:47:03,845
My Bala... We need to do this.

1128
01:47:04,646 --> 01:47:07,365
I will do this for the
state and for my people...

1129
01:47:08,366 --> 01:47:09,765
...I spent my years for.

1130
01:47:09,766 --> 01:47:14,205
Don't worry. My lineage will continue. My
children and grandchildren will follow me.

1131
01:47:14,206 --> 01:47:15,725
They will all follow us.

1132
01:47:15,726 --> 01:47:18,245
Our state will exist forever.

1133
01:47:18,766 --> 01:47:20,245
-Boran.
-My Bey.

1134
01:47:20,326 --> 01:47:22,765
They are keeping Orhan at Cam Valley, right?

1135
01:47:22,766 --> 01:47:25,245
My Bey, even though those
dogs covered my eyes...

1136
01:47:25,246 --> 01:47:29,565
...I kept the rivers and
the rocky roads in my mind.

1137
01:47:29,886 --> 01:47:32,245
They are keeping my Shahzade at Cam Valley.

1138
01:47:34,366 --> 01:47:35,605
Now..

1139
01:47:37,446 --> 01:47:39,725
...I will take the antidote from Ulugan...

1140
01:47:40,606 --> 01:47:42,285
...and surrender to him.

1141
01:47:42,766 --> 01:47:47,553
And he will probably take me to
the capital city of Sogut or Yenisehir.

1142
01:47:47,565 --> 01:47:49,165
What about my brother?

1143
01:47:49,166 --> 01:47:54,125
You will raid the Mongol
headquarters after me and take Orhan.

1144
01:47:54,286 --> 01:47:56,125
And in that time..

1145
01:47:56,526 --> 01:47:58,365
...the people will have healed.

1146
01:47:58,526 --> 01:48:00,565
But the actual duty...

1147
01:48:01,086 --> 01:48:02,805
...belongs to Samil.

1148
01:48:03,446 --> 01:48:05,445
You will come after me.

1149
01:48:06,326 --> 01:48:11,125
You will attack Ulugan in Sogut or Yenisehir...

1150
01:48:11,966 --> 01:48:13,445
...when he least expects it.

1151
01:48:14,006 --> 01:48:15,285
As you order, my Bey.

1152
01:48:15,286 --> 01:48:18,205
I will kill that infidel before anyone sees me.

1153
01:48:18,766 --> 01:48:22,965
My Bey, why don't we
kill that dog in our tribe...

1154
01:48:22,966 --> 01:48:25,645
..when he is on the way here?

1155
01:48:25,646 --> 01:48:27,765
No, I cannot risk my people's lives.

1156
01:48:27,766 --> 01:48:33,485
First, they will take the antidote and
they will heal. We need to know this.

1157
01:48:33,486 --> 01:48:34,565
Okay, my Bey.

1158
01:48:34,566 --> 01:48:38,605
And you, after taking Orhan,
will come to me with horsemen.

1159
01:48:38,846 --> 01:48:41,605
-As you order my Bey.
-As you order my Bey.

1160
01:48:44,966 --> 01:48:46,165
Beys

1161
01:48:46,606 --> 01:48:48,005
Brothers!

1162
01:48:48,366 --> 01:48:50,365
We are going to Sogut!

1163
01:48:50,686 --> 01:48:56,285
We will make these Mongol dogs
regret that they have stepped on our lands.

1164
01:48:56,286 --> 01:48:59,045
Allah is the Greatest!
Allah is the Greatest!

1165
01:49:14,406 --> 01:49:19,325
You cannot do this!

1166
01:49:28,766 --> 01:49:30,165
Come on Osman.

1167
01:49:30,926 --> 01:49:32,805
Start speaking.

1168
01:49:33,046 --> 01:49:35,285
Tell them that you bowed down to Mongols.

1169
01:49:35,286 --> 01:49:37,325
Then kneel.

1170
01:49:48,126 --> 01:49:50,685
Why don't you speak? Come on!

1171
01:50:01,206 --> 01:50:06,885
Samil... What are you trying to do, Osman?

1172
01:50:10,006 --> 01:50:11,365
Or people...

1173
01:50:13,926 --> 01:50:16,685
I hear those who say "Osman Bey...

1174
01:50:18,126 --> 01:50:20,765
...gave up his state for our lives.'

1175
01:50:21,006 --> 01:50:22,245
I hear them.

1176
01:50:23,246 --> 01:50:25,045
You should know..

1177
01:50:25,086 --> 01:50:29,405
I never gave up on my people...

1178
01:50:29,406 --> 01:50:33,205
...or our state which we
established with all those sufferings.

1179
01:50:33,206 --> 01:50:34,725
Is that so?

1180
01:50:34,766 --> 01:50:38,725
Do you think everything is over
because you have the antidote?

1181
01:50:38,806 --> 01:50:40,405
But you are wrong.

1182
01:50:42,166 --> 01:50:46,285
We will never stop before Ulugan dog dies!

1183
01:50:48,886 --> 01:50:49,325
Now!

1184
01:51:11,726 --> 01:51:13,565
We better leave, Lukas.

1185
01:51:14,286 --> 01:51:17,205
Come on.

1186
01:51:21,046 --> 01:51:24,685
Don't kill him! I have a better plan for him!

1187
01:51:26,846 --> 01:51:30,925
So this was all a game, Osman?

1188
01:51:30,966 --> 01:51:34,845
You wanted to set a trap and kill me...
-What did you think?

1189
01:51:34,886 --> 01:51:37,365
What did you think, you dog?

1190
01:51:37,486 --> 01:51:42,525
Did you think I'd bow down to you?

1191
01:51:42,526 --> 01:51:46,045
I will not kill you Osman.

1192
01:51:46,646 --> 01:51:48,445
I will not kill you.

1193
01:51:48,566 --> 01:51:54,765
I will kill your child Orhan in front of
you as a price for what you've done.

1194
01:52:03,086 --> 01:52:06,285
The spy that Osman placed in your castle.

1195
01:52:07,086 --> 01:52:08,845
Was his name Ilbay?

1196
01:52:09,886 --> 01:52:12,925
He was the one who saved Ulugan's life.

1197
01:52:15,286 --> 01:52:16,525
I saw him.

1198
01:52:17,286 --> 01:52:18,525
Ilbay?

1199
01:52:21,086 --> 01:52:22,765
We will learn, Sofia.

1200
01:52:22,766 --> 01:52:26,485
We will learn what they are trying to do.

1201
01:52:29,166 --> 01:52:32,325
Commander Ulugan, Turks raided our headquarters.

1202
01:52:33,406 --> 01:52:35,605
They took Orhan from us.

1203
01:52:41,086 --> 01:52:42,565
He really is his father's son.

1204
01:52:42,886 --> 01:52:45,605
So you saved your son, huh, Osman?

1205
01:52:45,886 --> 01:52:46,805
So?

1206
01:52:47,566 --> 01:52:49,405
What will happen to your Hatun?

1207
01:52:49,406 --> 01:52:52,445
What will happen to your children and people?

1208
01:52:52,446 --> 01:52:54,885
Who will save them from my hands?

1209
01:52:55,166 --> 01:52:58,125
I will...

1210
01:52:58,126 --> 01:53:02,965
I will drown you in your own blood... I will...

1211
01:53:03,446 --> 01:53:07,925
...cut you into pieces. Into pieces!

1212
01:53:08,446 --> 01:53:10,285
You heard, Altuga.

1213
01:53:11,126 --> 01:53:15,325
Kill everyone in the Kayi tribe!

1214
01:53:15,326 --> 01:53:16,525
Nokers (Mongolian Soldier)!

1215
01:53:16,526 --> 01:53:20,125
Let go!

1216
01:53:20,126 --> 01:53:25,365
Do you think this will stop me?
Do you think this will stop me?

1217
01:53:29,086 --> 01:53:31,605
Don't worry!

1218
01:53:32,086 --> 01:53:35,565
Allah is with us!

1219
01:53:47,126 --> 01:53:50,285
The antidote is showing
its effect, thanks to Allah.

1220
01:53:50,326 --> 01:53:53,643
The patients in the healing
tent also started getting up.

1221
01:53:53,655 --> 01:53:54,765
Thanks to Allah.

1222
01:53:56,246 --> 01:53:59,245
The poison lost its effect, huh?

1223
01:54:01,606 --> 01:54:03,165
Thanks to Allah...

1224
01:54:03,566 --> 01:54:04,725
But...

1225
01:54:06,446 --> 01:54:09,685
...I keep seeing my father
whenever I close my eyes, mother.

1226
01:54:10,806 --> 01:54:11,645
For our lives..

1227
01:54:11,646 --> 01:54:15,005
Your lives, our people's lives...

1228
01:54:15,006 --> 01:54:17,965
...mean the well-being and
future of our state, my daughter.

1229
01:54:17,966 --> 01:54:20,845
If that's what our Osman
Bey deemed appropriate...

1230
01:54:21,886 --> 01:54:24,165
..then this is what we must do.

1231
01:54:24,166 --> 01:54:25,885
Still, I cannot wait here.

1232
01:54:26,206 --> 01:54:29,445
I am alright now! I will question those Mongols!

1233
01:54:29,446 --> 01:54:30,805
Stop...

1234
01:54:30,806 --> 01:54:34,765
My Allah... He is not even a meter
long, but he says he will question them...

1235
01:54:37,766 --> 01:54:39,085
Ghazi...

1236
01:54:39,566 --> 01:54:41,685
You have a duty here.

1237
01:54:41,766 --> 01:54:44,405
Who will protect us if you leave?

1238
01:54:45,926 --> 01:54:47,245
True.

1239
01:54:47,646 --> 01:54:51,885
Besides, our Shahzade's child is also here.

1240
01:54:52,286 --> 01:54:53,965
We cannot leave.

1241
01:54:55,406 --> 01:54:59,845
When Orhan comes back, I will
tell him about your heroism, Ghazi.

1242
01:55:00,526 --> 01:55:02,005
Swear?

1243
01:55:02,406 --> 01:55:04,685
Oh no!
We are done..

1244
01:55:05,326 --> 01:55:09,165
Now, he will keep talking about himself.

1245
01:55:13,326 --> 01:55:16,325
Now we will unite and resist.

1246
01:55:16,766 --> 01:55:21,125
We will protect each other and our people.

1247
01:55:21,566 --> 01:55:26,325
We will get over this trouble
together with Allah's permission.

1248
01:55:27,046 --> 01:55:31,685
-My Orhan and my Osman will come.
-They will come.

1249
01:55:33,406 --> 01:55:38,925
-We will ruin the games of those demons.
-God willing.

1250
01:55:39,046 --> 01:55:40,405
Osman Bey...

1251
01:55:40,486 --> 01:55:43,045
...won't give up easily.

1252
01:55:43,406 --> 01:55:46,805
He must have a plan, right,Bala Hatun?

1253
01:55:49,206 --> 01:55:51,205
Come, Meryem.

1254
01:55:59,286 --> 01:56:01,485
If the cruel have a plan...

1255
01:56:02,006 --> 01:56:04,085
...we also have one, my daughter.

1256
01:56:05,086 --> 01:56:07,445
Everything will be alright, God willing.

1257
01:56:07,966 --> 01:56:09,565
Are you feeling better?

1258
01:56:10,406 --> 01:56:11,525
I am.

1259
01:56:11,926 --> 01:56:13,445
Thanks to you.

1260
01:56:15,486 --> 01:56:16,685
Meryem.

1261
01:56:18,726 --> 01:56:22,645
You kept saying "Aunt when you were sick.

1262
01:56:24,326 --> 01:56:26,685
Do you have an aunt who lives far away?

1263
01:56:32,046 --> 01:56:33,285
Aunt?

1264
01:56:41,286 --> 01:56:42,965
...didn't have anyone..

1265
01:56:43,486 --> 01:56:45,925
...except for my grandmother, Bala Hatun.

1266
01:56:49,886 --> 01:56:51,805
Did I really say "aunt"

1267
01:56:56,166 --> 01:56:57,445
Yes.

1268
01:56:58,766 --> 01:57:02,285
But I guess you said that because of your fever.

1269
01:57:12,726 --> 01:57:16,525
Samil, what are you doing here?
-My Shahzade...

1270
01:57:16,526 --> 01:57:20,525
The situation is not good...
What happened Samil? Tell me!

1271
01:57:20,526 --> 01:57:24,005
Someone attacked me when I
was about to kill Ulugan, Orhan Bey...

1272
01:57:24,046 --> 01:57:25,565
I failed.

1273
01:57:25,966 --> 01:57:27,565
Who, brother? Tell me! Who?

1274
01:57:27,566 --> 01:57:29,245
I couldn't see his face..

1275
01:57:29,246 --> 01:57:31,285
...but he knew we'd kill Ulugan.

1276
01:57:31,286 --> 01:57:34,285
I barely saved my life to let you know.

1277
01:57:34,846 --> 01:57:36,205
Samil...

1278
01:57:36,406 --> 01:57:41,245
...is my father alright? Is he alright?
-He was, but...

1279
01:57:41,326 --> 01:57:43,605
Ulugan took an oath for revenge.

1280
01:57:43,606 --> 01:57:46,405
Nokers (Mongolian Soldier)
came and told him that you were abducted.

1281
01:57:46,486 --> 01:57:49,805
Now he is going to our tribe.
He said he would burn it down.

1282
01:57:49,806 --> 01:57:51,685
To the tribe! Now!

1283
01:58:31,526 --> 01:58:32,765
Ilbay...

1284
01:58:33,286 --> 01:58:35,365
Let's see what you are going to do now.

1285
01:58:45,286 --> 01:58:47,365
Move! Move!

1286
01:58:58,566 --> 01:59:00,245
I cannot help it anymore Ayse.

1287
01:59:00,246 --> 01:59:04,325
I will punish those Mongol dogs.

1288
01:59:04,926 --> 01:59:09,285
Alps' swords might be
taken, but I have mine here.

1289
01:59:10,406 --> 01:59:11,885
Ghazi stop!

1290
01:59:12,206 --> 01:59:13,485
Don't go!

1291
01:59:16,246 --> 01:59:19,445
Burn the tents Nokers(Mongolian Soldier)!

1292
01:59:19,446 --> 01:59:23,645
Don't show mercy!
-Mongols!

1293
01:59:39,606 --> 01:59:43,765
Meryem, take the children, go inside!

1294
01:59:43,766 --> 01:59:47,565
Hatuns! Attack!

1295
02:00:28,406 --> 02:00:32,725
Hang on Alps! Hang on!

1296
02:00:33,846 --> 02:00:37,165
We will send these dogs
away from our tribe! Come on!

1297
02:00:37,166 --> 02:00:38,325
Osman's Hatun!

1298
02:00:43,766 --> 02:00:48,085
Your family and people, for
whom you have chained yourself...

1299
02:00:48,086 --> 02:00:53,205
...to save their lives now
await death at the edge.

1300
02:00:53,326 --> 02:00:57,805
When we go there, I'll just look at your face.

1301
02:00:58,126 --> 02:01:06,205
When you are looking at the heads of
your Hatun, your children, your family...

1302
02:01:06,206 --> 02:01:09,765
..all of them..

1303
02:01:09,766 --> 02:01:13,605
I will just look at the
growing fire in your eyes.

1304
02:01:13,606 --> 02:01:18,885
Look at me, if you do
something bad to my family or...

1305
02:01:18,886 --> 02:01:23,525
...my people, I will fill your
eye sockets with blood.

1306
02:01:23,566 --> 02:01:26,085
Once I get rid of my chains...

1307
02:01:26,086 --> 02:01:30,205
Once I get rid of my chains, then you'll see.

1308
02:01:30,486 --> 02:01:32,285
Then you'll see.

1309
02:01:32,286 --> 02:01:39,325
I just care about who will rule
and who will die in Kayi tribe now.

1310
02:01:40,006 --> 02:01:45,045
Now think about what you'll see in your tribe.

1311
02:01:51,726 --> 02:01:53,045
Attack, alps!

1312
02:01:53,086 --> 02:01:54,245
Attack, Sisters!

1313
02:01:54,246 --> 02:01:55,925
Shed the blood of demons!

1314
02:02:22,526 --> 02:02:24,205
Fatma!

1315
02:02:32,406 --> 02:02:35,125
Meryem. Meryem.

1316
02:02:36,126 --> 02:02:38,685
Come on, come on.

1317
02:02:52,966 --> 02:02:54,725
Orhan.

1318
02:02:58,726 --> 02:03:00,845
Come to me.

1319
02:03:01,126 --> 02:03:03,645
Fight, warriors!

1320
02:03:09,246 --> 02:03:11,485
Come on! Come on!

1321
02:03:49,526 --> 02:03:53,285
Alps, show no mercy for those jackals!

1322
02:03:53,446 --> 02:03:55,885
Come on!

1323
02:04:08,326 --> 02:04:12,365
My Shahzade, watch out!

1324
02:04:13,926 --> 02:04:18,485
I won't let them win even if I have no hands!

1325
02:04:18,726 --> 02:04:20,965
Come on, warriors!

1326
02:04:59,926 --> 02:05:03,365
Holofira, Holofira.

1327
02:05:03,446 --> 02:05:06,085
Orhan, are you alright?

1328
02:05:07,526 --> 02:05:12,525
Your hand. What did they do to you?
-I'm fine.

1329
02:05:12,686 --> 02:05:15,725
I'll be good. Come on.

1330
02:05:25,606 --> 02:05:28,485
Everybody will get what they deserve.

1331
02:05:56,406 --> 02:05:59,045
This chair belongs to me now.

1332
02:06:13,086 --> 02:06:16,325
I will rule this state now, Osman.

1333
02:06:23,246 --> 02:06:25,645
I said you were strong.

1334
02:06:27,006 --> 02:06:28,725
I knew you would come.

1335
02:06:29,286 --> 02:06:31,845
You didn't prove me to be wrong, Begum Hatun.

1336
02:06:42,006 --> 02:06:44,365
Do you know what I will do next?

1337
02:06:49,606 --> 02:06:51,125
I do.

1338
02:06:51,646 --> 02:06:53,645
I saw this in my dream.

1339
02:06:54,366 --> 02:06:56,525
You will accept my offer.

1340
02:06:57,006 --> 02:06:58,885
You will be my wife.

1341
02:07:02,846 --> 02:07:05,045
Wife of Ilbay Bey,

1342
02:07:05,646 --> 02:07:07,765
...grandson of Sungur Tegin.

1343
02:07:11,886 --> 02:07:14,365
We will rule this state together.

1344
02:07:23,966 --> 02:07:26,445
Your dream was a good sign then.

1345
02:07:31,406 --> 02:07:33,805
I will marry you, Ilbay.

1346
02:07:51,806 --> 02:07:54,485
Look at those people...

1347
02:07:54,846 --> 02:07:58,005
...who take shelter under
the shadow of your tent.

1348
02:08:03,766 --> 02:08:09,325
They will all die because of your arrogance.

1349
02:08:10,526 --> 02:08:16,125
Even the bravest person will be
surprised by what I'm going to do to you.

1350
02:08:17,046 --> 02:08:21,485
Don't harm my tribe and people.

1351
02:08:23,006 --> 02:08:25,085
Kill me.

1352
02:08:27,406 --> 02:08:31,645
I won't kill you once but a thousand times.

1353
02:08:37,046 --> 02:08:42,365
You think you're in an oasis
in the hell pit you've fallen into.

1354
02:08:42,726 --> 02:08:47,685
I will take your head before
the blood in the tribe dries up.

1355
02:08:49,406 --> 02:08:51,085
Enough.

1356
02:08:52,246 --> 02:08:57,365
Don't you want to know who
died and who lives in your family?

1357
02:09:01,286 --> 02:09:06,445
If you have harmed a single one in my family,

1358
02:09:07,126 --> 02:09:11,885
..I will eat you this dark soil.

1359
02:09:13,006 --> 02:09:16,725
I will make birds and worms eat you.

1360
02:09:17,326 --> 02:09:20,485
Your people will be eaten by birds and worms.

1361
02:09:20,646 --> 02:09:23,685
They will eat their flesh and bones!

1362
02:09:24,686 --> 02:09:28,645
Then I will hold a feast in your tent.

1363
02:09:30,326 --> 02:09:34,045
Well... Let's not make birds and worms starve.

1364
02:09:34,126 --> 02:09:35,325
Move.

1365
02:10:07,286 --> 02:10:08,645
Cerkutay!

1366
02:10:15,006 --> 02:10:18,765
This is the end of Turks
you have become a dog for!

1367
02:10:18,766 --> 02:10:22,445
It's the day I will put a
leash around your neck!

1368
02:10:28,966 --> 02:10:31,765
Father, I'm here!

1369
02:10:32,206 --> 02:10:35,165
-I'm here, father!
-Ghazi.

1370
02:10:35,326 --> 02:10:37,125
Ghazi.

1371
02:10:37,246 --> 02:10:39,525
Ghazi, go away!

1372
02:10:42,926 --> 02:10:44,845
He takes after you.

1373
02:10:48,846 --> 02:10:53,205
-Father.
-I'll kill you and make him a noker for me.

1374
02:10:53,406 --> 02:10:57,405
Ghazi, go. Go! Go!
-Father, no!

1375
02:12:27,966 --> 02:12:30,445
Bala Hatun...

1376
02:12:42,526 --> 02:12:46,405
Alaaddin Bey!

1377
02:12:49,246 --> 02:12:54,285
My Shahzade! They are
too many. We're losing this.

1378
02:12:54,526 --> 02:12:58,485
Boran Bey, we have to leave
immediately. We can't hold anymore.

1379
02:12:58,566 --> 02:13:01,405
Take women and children away quickly! Come on!

1380
02:13:15,806 --> 02:13:21,085
Bala Hatun. Shahzade Alaaddin says
we should leave the tribe immediately.

1381
02:13:21,286 --> 02:13:25,485
-We'll take elders, women and children away.
-We're losing it, Boran.

1382
02:13:25,806 --> 02:13:28,685
They are too many. There is nothing to do.

1383
02:13:28,806 --> 02:13:31,245
Come on, come on!

1384
02:13:32,326 --> 02:13:33,605
Gonca!

1385
02:13:33,806 --> 02:13:37,565
You take the elders. Holofira
you gather the children.

1386
02:13:37,766 --> 02:13:41,165
Ulgen, sisters... We'll protect our people.

1387
02:13:41,366 --> 02:13:43,445
We'll get out of here alive.

1388
02:13:45,406 --> 02:13:47,365
Come on

1389
02:13:48,526 --> 02:13:50,645
Come on!

1390
02:13:54,646 --> 02:13:57,965
Brother! Brother!

1391
02:13:58,126 --> 02:14:02,245
Mother is taking people away. We have to leave!

1392
02:14:02,326 --> 02:14:05,725
-We can't stand anymore. We have to go!
-We aren't going anywhere!

1393
02:14:05,766 --> 02:14:08,445
Anywhere! I won't leave the tribe!

1394
02:14:08,606 --> 02:14:11,125
-Even at the cost of my life!
-Brother!

1395
02:14:11,206 --> 02:14:13,605
Come on! Come on!

1396
02:15:20,926 --> 02:15:23,485
My Shahzade, they destroyed our tribe!

1397
02:15:23,526 --> 02:15:25,965
They killed people! We have to go!

1398
02:15:25,966 --> 02:15:29,245
I won't leave my tribe to
those dastards! Come on!

1399
02:15:33,606 --> 02:15:37,205
Come on! Come on, warriors!

1400
02:15:37,206 --> 02:15:40,725
Hurry up! Go towards the woods!

1401
02:15:41,006 --> 02:15:43,725
Fatma! Fatma, hold her.

1402
02:15:43,886 --> 02:15:47,685
Hurry up! Run towards the woods!

1403
02:15:48,406 --> 02:15:51,645
Come on, come on. Go towards the woods.

1404
02:15:53,726 --> 02:15:55,525
No, I can't go.

1405
02:15:55,806 --> 02:15:58,925
-I will make them pay for this!
-Ghazi, stop.

1406
02:16:10,726 --> 02:16:13,205
Die, you heathens!

1407
02:16:15,006 --> 02:16:16,725
Get off!

1408
02:16:16,806 --> 02:16:20,005
-Ghazi?
-Get off!

1409
02:16:20,486 --> 02:16:23,565
Come on, faster!

1410
02:16:24,166 --> 02:16:26,605
Leave me, dastard!

1411
02:16:28,646 --> 02:16:30,845
What have you done, Ghazi?

1412
02:17:00,245 --> 02:17:03,683
My Shahzade. We need to go.

1413
02:17:03,886 --> 02:17:06,965
-The tribe has fallen.
-I won't leave!

1414
02:17:24,325 --> 02:17:28,725
My Shahzade. My Shahzade, we have to go.

1415
02:17:29,126 --> 02:17:30,924
-My Shahzade.
-Boran, leave me!

1416
02:17:30,966 --> 02:17:35,285
My Shahzade! It's over! It's over!

1417
02:17:35,325 --> 02:17:38,205
It's over, my Shahzade.

1418
02:17:43,566 --> 02:17:47,725
It's over, my Shahzade. Don't you
see? Remember what our Bey said.

1419
02:17:48,566 --> 02:17:52,924
For our state to live forever, you have to live.

1420
02:17:53,966 --> 02:17:57,245
The land might be lost, but
the tradition remains, Orhan Bey.

1421
02:17:57,406 --> 02:18:00,645
Brother, we have to go now. Boran Bey is right.

1422
02:18:00,646 --> 02:18:03,924
The land might be lost, but
the tradition remains. Come on.

1423
02:18:03,924 --> 02:18:05,805
Come on!

1424
02:18:05,806 --> 02:18:08,683
Come on! -We are going back!

1425
02:18:08,686 --> 02:18:11,525
Come on Alps!

1426
02:18:11,526 --> 02:18:17,325
Come on!

1427
02:19:03,366 --> 02:19:06,125
This is the end, Yusuf...

1428
02:19:24,726 --> 02:19:29,205
We will come back for sure. For sure.

1429
02:19:39,165 --> 02:19:40,965
Brother..

1430
02:19:44,004 --> 02:19:45,763
Come on brother.

1431
02:20:46,886 --> 02:20:47,365
What..

1432
02:20:47,366 --> 02:20:48,005
What...

1433
02:20:49,326 --> 02:20:50,805
...did you do to my tribe...

1434
02:20:52,246 --> 02:20:53,725
...to my people...

1435
02:20:53,726 --> 02:20:55,405
...to my sons...

1436
02:20:55,406 --> 02:20:57,565
...to my children?

1437
02:20:57,886 --> 02:20:59,805
You faithless dogs!

1438
02:21:00,126 --> 02:21:01,725
What did you do?

1439
02:21:03,126 --> 02:21:05,165
How could you hurt them?!

1440
02:21:05,446 --> 02:21:09,125
What did they do to you?!

1441
02:21:27,246 --> 02:21:32,245
My tent...

1442
02:21:32,686 --> 02:21:37,445
You killed my people, my innocent people.

1443
02:21:37,806 --> 02:21:44,005
Faithless dogs!

1444
02:21:49,206 --> 02:21:51,765
Faithless dog!

1445
02:21:59,966 --> 02:22:01,005
Ulugan!

1446
02:22:03,086 --> 02:22:04,125
Ulugan!

1447
02:22:07,926 --> 02:22:13,165
Come! Face me! Come on!

1448
02:22:13,166 --> 02:22:14,965
Come on!

1449
02:22:15,166 --> 02:22:17,725
Face me! Come on!

1450
02:22:44,846 --> 02:22:46,805
Ulugan!

1451
02:22:52,766 --> 02:22:56,485
Let go! Let go!

1452
02:23:08,926 --> 02:23:10,645
You are done, Osman!

1453
02:23:10,686 --> 02:23:12,445
Your state is destroyed Your tradition...

1454
02:23:12,446 --> 02:23:13,845
Your state is destroyed!
Your tradition...

1455
02:23:14,166 --> 02:23:17,485
...your banner, they are all under my feet now!

1456
02:23:17,486 --> 02:23:20,205
The Sky Wolf Osman is destroyed now!

1457
02:23:20,686 --> 02:23:22,365
You no longer exist!

1458
02:23:22,886 --> 02:23:26,485
You did this to my state and to my people...

1459
02:23:26,526 --> 02:23:30,725
If I don't punish you for this...

1460
02:23:30,926 --> 02:23:35,965
...then may the blood of all
our martyrs be haram to me!

1461
02:23:39,566 --> 02:23:43,405
I will shed dark blood with dark steel...

1462
02:23:43,646 --> 02:23:47,285
...and water the dark soil with your blood!

1463
02:23:48,686 --> 02:23:51,645
May it come in clean and
come out covered in blood!

1464
02:23:52,846 --> 02:23:56,085
If I do not take an eye for
an eye, a tooth for a tooth...

1465
02:23:56,166 --> 02:23:58,205
...a life for a life..

1466
02:23:58,526 --> 02:24:01,805
...then may they not call me Osman Bey!